00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:20.660
Emergency!

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:22.960
Patrol car #503 calling headquarters...

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:23.960
Emergency...

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:25.330
Patrol 503, over

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:29.300
We found the criminals! They're in a stolen vehicle,

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.960
and are traveling along Sotobari and Gyoki roads.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:33.170
Roger.

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:37.300
Please State the license plate number of the suspects car, and what both the car and the suspects look like. Over.

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:38.720
Roger.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:40.720
It's a black SUV,

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:44.060
with plate number Shinzuku 500, SA 32-55.

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:46.150
And the suspects look like...

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:48.940
Lupin and Fujiko!

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:52.780
Patrol 503, please stop joking around.

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:54.530
I'm not joking...

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.580
Patrol car #503 calling headquarters...

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:02.790
Lupin is now turning off Gyoki Road onto Middle Road.

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:04.790
Patrol 503, just cut the crap already...

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:05.250
Over.

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:08.130
I told you, I'm being serious here!

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:12.130
Wait a second, Sato-san.

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:14.050
Please drive a little more carefully...

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:15.590
Shouldn't you still be contacting headquarters?

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:16.800
Ah... Yes!

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:19.220
Patrol #503 calling headquarters...

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:21.310
Suspects are turning right onto Harumi Road.

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:22.770
How dare you wear a lupin mask for a robbery...

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:24.180
I'll never forgive you for that!

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:32.440
Welcome, and good evening to you!

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:43.990
That'll be 1,237 yen.

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:52.130
Pull your car over now!

00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:59.470
What's going on?

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:00.850
Awesome!

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:02.890
Pull your car over now!

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:04.310
Let me repeat myself...

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:07.060
There's nowhere for you to run,

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:09.520
so pull your car over now!

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:18.200
You shouldn't have done that...

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:20.570
Now, I'll pay you back with an eye for an eye!

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:07.080
Sato-san, they're getting away!

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:09.040
Hold on to your seat.

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:15.290
Sato-san, what are you doing?

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:16.920
You'll bite your tongue if you keep talking...

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:29.140
Sa-Sato-san!

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:29.730
Just hold on!

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:37.400
Wa-wait, Sato-san!

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:50.540
Takagi-kun, contact headquarters.

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:51.580
Yes, ma'am!

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:57.290
Honestly...

00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:58.840
Sato-san,

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:01.840
Backup and ambulances are on their way.

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:03.380
This bastard has only himself to thank.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:08.220
How dare he wear the mask of my first love?

00:04:09.010 --> 00:04:11.180
F-first love?

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:12.770
Go and have a look at Fujiko.

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:13.730
Okay.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:20.690
Hang on! The ambulance will be here soon.

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:21.690
Sato-san!

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:23.240
Fujiko just fainted.

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:25.860
The injury isn't very serious.

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:26.870
Really?

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:32.160
But, why did they commit a robbery in such odd masks?

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:34.790
Koumi... Island...

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:36.080
Koumi Island?

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:40.170
Is that why you committed robbery, so that you could take a vacation on that island?

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:41.510
N-no...

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:43.050
No?

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:45.010
What about that island, then?

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:45.880
J-

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:46.720
J-Jolly...

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:50.680
Jolly Roger...

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:52.680
Jolly Roger?

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:54.310
Do you know what that is?

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:55.350
No idea...

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:12.700
Koumi Island

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:23.260
Mama! Hurry, hurry!

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:24.130
Let's go over there!

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:25.170
Wait for me!

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:28.050
Hey, do you know how to use this?

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:29.180
Let me show you.

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:31.640
Sensei, what kind  of fish are here?

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:40.060
Good morning! may I have the name you made reservations under?

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:43.610
Mouri Kogoro, the famous detective.

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:46.990
We have two adults, two students, and five children.

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:48.990
Let me look you up.

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:57.830
You know how the 'Daily Times' publishes a puzzle to solve each week, right?

00:05:57.830 --> 00:05:59.330
They're really hard!

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:01.540
The cash prize keeps accumulating if no one sends in the right answer.

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:04.550
It even reached 300,000 yen!

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:08.630
And do you know who it was that won all that money...?

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:10.970
I have no idea...

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:12.720
Oh, you mean...

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:14.770
Bingo!

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:16.600
After all, I am a famous detective.

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:18.390
Puzzles are a piece of cake for me!

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:21.060
Although, I'm the one who told you the right answer...

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:24.690
If you have 300,000 yen, you can take a vacation in Paris.

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:28.950
The streets of Paris are just my style, but then I'd feel guilty having all the fun myself,

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:34.200
and it's not like we always have opportunities like this,

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:38.370
so I brought them along as well.

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:40.710
I'm just a really kind man, don't you think?

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:42.500
Y-yeah...

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:44.630
What are our room numbers then?

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:49.090
I'm sorry, but I couldn't find your reservation.

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:50.840
Are you serious?!?

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:52.220
Hey, hey...

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:54.180
Wait a minute,

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:56.100
I made this reservation a while ago!

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:59.480
But, I couldn't find your name on the reservation list.

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:02.150
Are we going to have to camp outside?

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:06.070
This island has a tropical climate, so there might be poisonous bugs all over the place.

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:08.240
If only we'd known that it'd end up like this...

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:10.860
Well, we'll think of something.

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:13.820
After all, it's not like we can't talk to people here.

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:16.240
Wow! Haibara-san sounds like an adult.

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:19.410
Well, I'm pretty sure she's not a child...

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:25.840
The front desk said that they'll contact the Tourism Division.

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:27.000
Sorry for all the trouble.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:28.960
But that man promised me!

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:32.300
He said the reservation was confirmed!

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:34.430
Well, I'm confused too.

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:36.720
Good afternoon, sorry to keep you waiting.

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:39.480
You must be Mouri Kogoro-san, the famous detective...

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:47.360
I apologize...

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:48.690
I'm Iwanaga from the Tourism Division.

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:53.110
Iwanaga Jouji
Koumi Island Tourism Division

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:53.240
The amount of tourists has just skyrocketed this month.

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:54.700
Hotels are all completely booked.

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:57.160
Seems all the happy travelers are causing busyness for us...

00:07:57.330 --> 00:08:00.830
But I already made your reservations for you.

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:04.120
You <i>are</i> the famous detective Mouri Kogoro, after all.

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:06.840
Please, follow me. This way.

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:09.250
What a dumbass...

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:10.510
What is he doing?

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:15.930
Who are they?

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:17.930
They're probably treasure hunters.

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:19.520
Treasure Hunters?

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:21.390
Do they repair pipes?

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:24.390
Flushing toilets and stuff like that?

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:28.570
That's not it, Genta-kun.

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:32.490
They look for treasure all over the world.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:37.200
But how do you know that they're treasure hunters?

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:39.240
Ah, just look at them.

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:43.160
Their skin is nicely tanned,

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:47.380
but only on their hands and heads, and not anywhere else, right?

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:50.000
They must wear wet suits a lot.

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:54.340
Plus the color of their hair has faded from prolonged contact with sea water.

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:57.140
But that only proves that they dive a lot.

00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:59.010
That may be true...

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:00.470
But, if you look at that poster,

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:02.390
You'll realize that my deduction is logical.

00:09:02.470 --> 00:09:05.440
 Koumi
Island

00:09:02.470 --> 00:09:05.440
The island that hides
 the sunken palace.

00:09:02.470 --> 00:09:05.440
Join us on this quest
 for the ancient treasure!

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:07.520
Treasure!!

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:08.480
Yeah.

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:10.770
They must be dreaming...

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:14.490
...of finding the treasure sleeping under the sea.

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:34.800
Jolly

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:34.800
Roger

00:09:30.790 --> 00:09:34.800
In The

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:34.800
Deep Azure

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:42.850
I'm high school detective, Kudo Shinichi.

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:45.480
Eh? You say I don't look like a high-schooler?

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:49.940
Original Creator      Aoyama Gosho

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:52.480
While visiting an amusement park with my
 childhood friend and classmate, Mouri Ran...

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:56.860
Screenplay    Hiroshi Kawashiabara

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:58.740
I went to investigate, and witnessed a man in black in the middle of a suspicious transaction.

00:09:57.820 --> 00:10:01.490
Music    Katsuo Ohno

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:02.200
Engrossed in watching the deal,

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:04.700
I didn't notice his partner sneaking up behind me.

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:06.710
Character Design        Sudou Masatomo

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:11.250
Art Director     Shibuya Yukihiro
Color Planning       Nishi Kayoko

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:12.670
I was forced to take a poison, and when I woke up...

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:15.670
My body had shrunk!

00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:19.680
Director of Photography     Nomura Takashi
Sound Director               Izawa Motoi

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:19.010
If they found out that Kudo Shinichi was still alive,

00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:21.930
They would come after me again and endanger the lives of those around me.

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:25.680
Edogawa Conan     Takayama Minami

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:25.850
Following Prof. Agasa advice I decided to hide my identity.

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:29.770
When Ran asked me who I was, I blurted out, "Edogawa Conan".

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:29.600
Conan  Doyle Best


00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:29.600
Edogawa Ranpo -Complete Works

00:10:30.310 --> 00:10:32.310
In order to find more information on the men in black,

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:34.980
I moved in with Ran and her father, who is a detective.

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:38.200
Mouri Kogoro         Kamiya Akira
Mouri Ran      Yamazaki Wakana

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:41.410
Yes, this old man is Ran's Father, the "famous detective", Mouri Kogoro.

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:44.620
People call him "Sleeping Kogoro",

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:49.750
but that's because... that's what's really happening.

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:53.670
Her name is Suzuki Sonoko,

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:57.460
Suzuki Sonoko    Matsui Naoko
 Professor Agasa    Ogata Kenichi

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:55.710
She's Ran classmate.

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:59.630
By looking, you'd never know she comes from a wealthy family, since she's a rather easy-going girl.

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:02.470
This man is professor Agasa

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:08.520
Professor Agasa has invented a lot of interesting and unique gadgets for me since my body has shrunk.

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:14.020
This girl is Haibara Ai.

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:18.190
Haibara Ai        Hayashibara Megumi

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:16.730
Her true identity is Miyano Shiho.

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:21.240
She used to be a member of the black Organization, but in order to escape,

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:26.950
She swallowed the same poison that I was given, and her body shrank as well.

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:32.500
Producers

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:32.500
Suwa Michihiko
Yoshioka Masahito

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:32.500
I still don't know the true identities of those men in black,

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:35.960
But I bet on my name as a detective, I'll have it out with them one day.

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:41.510
Director       Yamamoto Yasuichiro

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:39.550
Even though I've become small,

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:41.720
My mind is still that of a great detective.

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:45.390
There is only one truth!

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:52.440
Speaking of which...

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:56.440
Why are treasure hunters coming on this island?

00:11:56.820 --> 00:12:00.240
Someone found some treasure two weeks ago.

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:01.700
Treasure?

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:06.370
I heard that they found silver in Seabed Palace. Is that true?

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:08.160
I think so.

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:09.950
What's Seabed Palace?

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:13.210
See that deserted island over there?

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:15.500
It's Yorioya Island.

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:17.250
Yorioya Island

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:19.300
200 meters east of the island,

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:23.300
there are ruins in the seabed.

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:30.220
Ten years ago, there was a rumor saying 
that there were ruins near Koumi Island.

00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:33.980
Many scholars came to do a research on it,

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:37.060
Seabed Palace

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:38.820
but they never concluded whether it's man-made or natural.

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:43.780
Yorioya Island used to be exposed above water.

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:48.620
300 Years ago, earthquakes caused it to sink into the ocean depths.

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:50.490
Due to earthquakes?

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:52.200
Like in a landslide?

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:58.080
Yes, I heard that the seabed nearby contains methane hydrate.

00:12:58.590 --> 00:13:01.250
The earthquakes disturbed it and caused a landslide.

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:04.340
That's the most logical explanation so far.

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:07.010
Hey Conan...

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:10.470
What's "meat-tanned-hand-maid?"

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:13.140
Methane hydrate.

00:13:12.680 --> 00:13:20.110
Methane Hydrate

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:16.230
In a low temperature, high pressure environment,

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:19.940
Water combines with methane and forms a kind of cage.

00:13:20.570 --> 00:13:22.480
It's also called combustible ice.

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:24.110
Combustible Ice?

00:13:24.110 --> 00:13:25.820
Water cage?

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:27.610
I don't get it at all.

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:30.830
To put it simply,

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:33.410
you've built a house of cards before, right?

00:13:33.410 --> 00:13:36.710
Water builds a house like that,

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:40.130
and each room contains methane.

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:45.420
If the temperature rises or the pressure falls,

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:49.090
it'll become unstable, and the whole thing will collapse, releasing the methane.

00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:50.300
I see!

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:55.770
That's why the island, being held up by methane, lost its support and cause a landslide.

00:13:56.810 --> 00:13:59.060
Something like that.

00:14:02.070 --> 00:14:04.320
I learned that from what they said on TV...

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:06.950
Oh, I see...

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:10.820
Idiot...

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:14.580
Excuse me, Mima-san?

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:16.450
This is Iwanaga from the Tourism Division.

00:14:16.450 --> 00:14:19.880
Mima-san, are you here? Mima-san?

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:22.540
It's so different from the hotel.

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:23.340
I know...

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:29.300
I'm sorry. He must not be here right now.

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:30.720
I just tried calling for him.

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:32.260
What's all the noise for?

00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:33.680
Oh, Mima-san!

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:36.390
This is Mouri-san and his guests, of whom I told you about over the phone.

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:37.560
Mima Kasuo
Landlord of "Koumi Inn" Lodge

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:39.020
Two rooms and meals for one night, 5000 yen.

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:40.520
Take it or leave it.

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:42.110
Wait a minute, Mima-san!

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:43.820
What a rude guy...

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:46.190
Sorry, he's really a good man,

00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:47.990
but he can be a bit weird sometimes.

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:52.370
So Who's participating in the treasure hunt?

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:53.910
We are!

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:55.870
We are!

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:58.710
You two young ladies are planning to go diving, right?

00:14:58.710 --> 00:14:59.370
Yes.

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:02.580
I can give you a ride if you want to go right now.

00:15:02.580 --> 00:15:04.040
We'd like that, please.

00:15:04.420 --> 00:15:06.210
What about the two of you?

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:09.010
Treasure hunting is fun.

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:11.930
I want to relax. Don't worry about me.

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:13.180
What about Mouri-san?

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:14.430
Want to go treas-

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:15.140
No thanks.

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:19.940
Just tell me where I can buy drinks and find
 beautiful hostesses at the same time.

00:15:26.520 --> 00:15:29.530
Mouri Ran-san and Suzuki Sonoko-san, right?

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:30.490
Mabuchi Chika
 Owner of "The Grotto" Diving Equipment Shop

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:32.320
Would you like to rent the whole set?

00:15:32.320 --> 00:15:33.240
Yep!

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:34.410
Kimiko!

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:40.790
Yamakuchi Kimiko
 Diving Instructor

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:38.120
You two...

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:40.330
Will these wets suites work for you?

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:43.170
I think Size M should fit you.

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:44.000
Yes!

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:45.040
Those are perfect.

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:46.340
Great!

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:49.760
To be honest, we don't have a very big selection of wet suits here.

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:52.090
Really? Sorry to trouble you in finding these, then.

00:15:52.090 --> 00:15:54.090
These wet suits look so nice!

00:15:54.090 --> 00:15:55.350
You think so?

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:56.640
Excuse me!

00:15:56.640 --> 00:16:00.730
Hey, clean up after you're done!

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:02.940
We'll be back.

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:09.480
They're treasure hunters, right?

00:16:09.480 --> 00:16:11.030
Are they going to be our diving partners?

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:14.990
No, they just came to borrow our air compressor.

00:16:14.990 --> 00:16:18.160
There have been a lot of them recently, which causes us a lot of trouble.

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:21.290
Is it because of the silver that was found?

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:28.340
There's a legend saying that Anne escaped from the jail and hid her treasure on this island.

00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:29.460
Who's Anne?

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:30.260
That's her.

00:16:31.630 --> 00:16:36.760
270 years ago, during the Kyoto Era of the Edo period,

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:40.430
The Seabed Palace was still above ground.

00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:45.980
Two rare artifacts were found at Seabed Palace,

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:49.400
a cutlass and a pistol.

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:53.490
According  to the initials on the cutlass and the pistol,

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:58.580
These weapons used to belong to two female pirates who were active around 1730,

00:16:58.580 --> 00:17:02.370
Whose names were Anne Bonny and Mary Read.

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:06.370
They were led by captain Jack Rickman.

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:09.380
They were female pirates?

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:10.500
That's right.

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:16.510
Anne Bonny and Mary Read were pirates under Captain Jack.

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:20.060
But when they were attacked by the English Navy,

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:28.020
all the crewmen hid below deck while the two women fought bravery back-to-back.

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:30.570
Back-to-back?

00:17:30.570 --> 00:17:34.150
Yes... The idea is to let your partner watch your back,

00:17:34.150 --> 00:17:37.200
so that you can concentrate on the enemy before you.

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:39.870
If either person lacked trust in the other, it wouldn't work.

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:43.410
Ran, You're...

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:47.830
Ran, You're... You're the only one I trust to watch my back.

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:50.290
S-Sonoko...

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:53.000
Just kidding!

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:55.800
But, you want Shinichi-kun to watch your back, don't you?

00:17:56.260 --> 00:17:58.010
I don't care about him.

00:17:58.010 --> 00:17:59.260
<i>Really?</i>

00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:01.010
Yes, really!

00:18:02.310 --> 00:18:07.390
Anne escaped from her prison in the Bahamas and moved to the Pacific Ocean.

00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:12.020
She continued as a pirate and waited for Mary to escape from prison as well.

00:18:12.020 --> 00:18:14.230
Many years later, this story was confirmed,

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:19.910
causing a legend about the two hiding their treasure on Koumi Island.

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:24.160
So, let's go look for Anne and Mary's treasure!

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:27.370
Are these real?

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:29.170
Who knows?

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:31.880
If they are, protecting them must cause a lot of trouble...

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:35.510
Maybe they were made just to publicize this island.

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:39.220
That would cause even more trouble.

00:18:39.590 --> 00:18:41.510
Seems like they cause trouble either way.

00:18:41.850 --> 00:18:43.350
Sorry, sorry!

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:44.850
Sorry to keep you waiting-

00:18:46.060 --> 00:18:47.730
Hey, hey...

00:18:48.180 --> 00:18:50.730
Here. This is the map for the treasure hunt.

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:58.240
Starting here, you want to go to each of the five points on the map, solve their riddles, and collect the stamp from each area.

00:18:58.820 --> 00:19:01.070
This is the first point.

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:04.240
Take the stamp and stamp it on the blank space here,

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:08.750
then take a hint card for the next point from the treasure chest there.

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:11.120
This game's just a way to keep kids occupied.

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:12.710
Don't say that.

00:19:12.710 --> 00:19:14.710
Everyone looks so enthusiastic about it.

00:19:14.710 --> 00:19:16.590
10 and 12...

00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:19.380
This is the key to finding the treasure.

00:19:19.380 --> 00:19:21.260
The clue for the next point is...

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:24.470
even near the end of the sunset,
a pirate still shines

00:19:21.260 --> 00:19:24.760
"Even near the end of the sunset, a pirate still shines."

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:26.310
What does that mean?

00:19:26.310 --> 00:19:28.140
Well, do your best!

00:19:28.140 --> 00:19:31.600
You'll get a present if you find the treasure!

00:19:31.600 --> 00:19:35.060
Is the present an all-you-eat-buffet?

00:19:35.060 --> 00:19:37.650
You'll know once you solve all the riddles.

00:19:37.650 --> 00:19:39.530
Alright, I have to work really hard now!

00:19:39.530 --> 00:19:42.240
You don't even know if that's the prize yet...

00:19:42.240 --> 00:19:43.530
Hey, Uncle!

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:45.070
Yes, What?

00:19:45.070 --> 00:19:48.370
Did you think of these riddles yourself?

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:50.870
Eh? Kind of...

00:19:50.870 --> 00:19:52.330
Oh, by the way,

00:19:52.330 --> 00:19:56.040
There's a place you can rent bikes next door.

00:19:56.040 --> 00:19:58.300
You'll be really tired if you walk, so take a bike.

00:19:58.300 --> 00:19:59.510
Okay!

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:04.800
I can see you're enthusiastic about this too, Kudo-kun!

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:25.490
Alright, you're all set!

00:20:25.490 --> 00:20:30.410
Just follow Kimiko's instructions and have a safe, fun dive!

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:33.870
Watch out of the area south of Seabed Palace,

00:20:33.870 --> 00:20:35.500
it's really deep over there.

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:37.250
Please don't scare us.

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:41.050
Don't worry, I'll be with you.

00:20:41.050 --> 00:20:42.260
You're right.

00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:43.930
Please take care of us!

00:22:58.270 --> 00:22:59.600
That was quick.

00:22:59.600 --> 00:23:00.600
Did something happen?

00:23:00.940 --> 00:23:01.940
Sharks!

00:23:04.570 --> 00:23:06.730
Since the riddle mentioned the sunset,

00:23:06.730 --> 00:23:09.950
we came to the west side of the island,

00:23:09.950 --> 00:23:12.660
but where's the treasure box with the next hint?

00:23:14.330 --> 00:23:16.120
Oh! I got it!

00:23:16.700 --> 00:23:21.870
The hint was... "Even near the end of the sunset, a pirate still shines", right?

00:23:21.870 --> 00:23:23.380
So that must mean...

00:23:23.920 --> 00:23:25.170
It's out there!

00:23:25.170 --> 00:23:26.750
Really?

00:23:26.750 --> 00:23:27.960
And then what?

00:23:29.380 --> 00:23:32.390
You mean the stamp is in the middle of the ocean?

00:23:33.470 --> 00:23:35.220
I guess that's not it after all...

00:23:36.310 --> 00:23:37.810
Oh, I see...

00:23:38.850 --> 00:23:40.270
Look over there!

00:23:40.270 --> 00:23:41.980
What is that?

00:23:41.980 --> 00:23:43.520
It's a large school of fish.

00:23:43.520 --> 00:23:45.520
Are there any eel there?

00:23:45.520 --> 00:23:47.780
There wouldn't be any eel here...

00:23:47.780 --> 00:23:49.240
Now I understand!

00:23:49.650 --> 00:23:50.900
Hey, Conan!

00:23:52.070 --> 00:23:54.490
Why is it that <i>you're</i> always saying, "I understand, I understand?"

00:23:54.490 --> 00:23:56.330
What did you figure out?

00:24:11.630 --> 00:24:14.680
Do you know why fish always swim in groups?

00:24:14.680 --> 00:24:16.260
Well...

00:24:16.260 --> 00:24:18.180
So they can play together?

00:24:18.180 --> 00:24:21.600
Or maybe they get together to eat because they're hungry.

00:24:21.600 --> 00:24:22.520
Bingo!

00:24:22.770 --> 00:24:24.900
So, what is it that fish eat?

00:24:25.310 --> 00:24:27.480
Plankton?

00:24:27.480 --> 00:24:28.570
Exactly.

00:24:32.030 --> 00:24:33.450
Amazing!

00:24:36.410 --> 00:24:38.450
Is there anything down here?

00:24:38.450 --> 00:24:39.330
Just look here.

00:24:43.960 --> 00:24:45.920
It's bio-luminescent plankton!

00:24:45.920 --> 00:24:46.960
I got it!

00:24:46.960 --> 00:24:50.050
"Even near the end of the sunset, a pirate still shines."

00:24:50.050 --> 00:24:51.880
That must mean this is the place!

00:24:51.880 --> 00:24:53.050
Found it.

00:24:56.890 --> 00:24:57.050
A skinny pirate would just laugh.

00:24:57.050 --> 00:24:58.260
A skinny pirate would just laugh.

00:24:58.720 --> 00:25:01.310
"A skinny pirate would just laugh."

00:25:01.560 --> 00:25:04.190
You can laugh even if you're not thin.

00:25:09.020 --> 00:25:10.730
What's wrong, Haibara?

00:25:10.730 --> 00:25:15.240
I saw someone in a wet suit, covered in blood, being carried away.

00:25:15.240 --> 00:25:16.160
What?

00:25:16.530 --> 00:25:19.030
I don't know if it Ran-san or not, though.

00:25:19.030 --> 00:25:20.160
Conan-kun!

00:25:20.830 --> 00:25:23.290
I have to leave with Edogawa-kun for a while,

00:25:23.290 --> 00:25:25.210
so you guys continue on without us.

00:25:25.210 --> 00:25:26.670
Why is Haibara-san leaving too?

00:25:26.670 --> 00:25:30.130
Don't worry, I'm still here!

00:25:30.130 --> 00:25:33.050
We can find the treasure by ourselves.

00:25:33.550 --> 00:25:34.880
You're right.

00:25:49.560 --> 00:25:51.730
Ran-Ran-neechan!

00:25:51.730 --> 00:25:53.190
Conan-kun!

00:25:53.190 --> 00:25:54.400
Ai-chan's here too?

00:25:54.940 --> 00:25:56.320
Are you okay?

00:25:56.900 --> 00:25:58.360
We're fine.

00:26:00.280 --> 00:26:03.830
Officer Uehira
Koumi Island Resident Policeman

00:26:01.370 --> 00:26:03.740
How is it, Uehira-san?

00:26:03.740 --> 00:26:04.830
Kimi-chan!

00:26:04.830 --> 00:26:06.710
Were you there too?

00:26:07.710 --> 00:26:11.170
I was guiding my clients for a dive nearby.

00:26:11.170 --> 00:26:15.510
But I was shocked when I heard that sharks were attacking people.

00:26:15.510 --> 00:26:19.840
It's strange how there were three of them, but only one was attacked.

00:26:19.840 --> 00:26:21.100
What are you getting at?

00:26:21.430 --> 00:26:22.810
Nothing.

00:26:22.810 --> 00:26:24.640
But it's so troubling...

00:26:24.640 --> 00:26:27.730
It's been a long time since the last accident.

00:26:27.730 --> 00:26:31.560
Speaking of which, this is the first time I've seen sharks at that spot.

00:26:38.740 --> 00:26:39.990
What is it?

00:26:39.990 --> 00:26:45.790
Kimiko-san said there were three of them diving together, but only one was attacked.

00:26:45.790 --> 00:26:47.330
You don't think it was an accident?

00:26:47.330 --> 00:26:51.750
They should know how to deal with sharks since they're all professionals.

00:26:55.960 --> 00:26:57.050
What did you find?

00:26:57.970 --> 00:26:59.590
A plastic bag.

00:27:02.800 --> 00:27:04.560
Fish blood?

00:27:04.560 --> 00:27:06.270
So that's the reason...

00:27:06.270 --> 00:27:07.270
Yeah.

00:27:07.270 --> 00:27:10.350
Take fish blood, seal it in a plastic bag,

00:27:10.350 --> 00:27:13.110
and hide it in the jacket of the swim suit.

00:27:13.560 --> 00:27:17.320
Underwater, atmospheric pressure increases by one for every 10 meters,

00:27:17.320 --> 00:27:19.740
and sea level is already at one atmospheric pressure.

00:27:19.740 --> 00:27:22.030
It become two when you dive 10 meters,

00:27:22.030 --> 00:27:24.080
and four when you get to 30 meters.

00:27:24.530 --> 00:27:30.960
With such a high water pressure weighing down on it, the plastic bag would eventually burst.

00:27:31.790 --> 00:27:34.380
Sharks can hear noises from miles away,

00:27:35.090 --> 00:27:39.510
and can smell blood from even farther.

00:27:50.890 --> 00:27:52.480
This is a murder case.

00:27:52.480 --> 00:27:55.190
Yes, although it's not over yet.

00:27:55.190 --> 00:27:57.440
Hey, you brats!

00:27:57.440 --> 00:28:01.280
What're you two doing here?

00:28:01.280 --> 00:28:02.950
Uncle, a case happened!

00:28:02.950 --> 00:28:04.530
What?

00:28:04.530 --> 00:28:07.370
Why don't they ever contact me first...

00:28:13.040 --> 00:28:16.790
'Cuz I'm the famous detective, Mouri Kogoro.

00:28:21.760 --> 00:28:23.970
A shark's mouth sure is big...

00:28:23.970 --> 00:28:29.680
The thing is... being bitten by a shark isn't a case, it's an accident.

00:28:36.150 --> 00:28:38.270
I don't see anything over there...

00:28:38.270 --> 00:28:39.650
Huh? What's this?

00:28:47.450 --> 00:28:49.790
How is he, Doctor?

00:28:49.790 --> 00:28:51.660
I did everything I could,

00:28:51.660 --> 00:28:54.250
but it was too late.

00:28:54.250 --> 00:28:55.670
I'm sorry...

00:28:55.670 --> 00:28:56.790
Damn!

00:28:56.790 --> 00:28:58.170
No way...

00:28:58.170 --> 00:29:00.250
How could this accident happen?

00:29:00.250 --> 00:29:02.880
It's not an accident.

00:29:06.390 --> 00:29:08.010
You're the famous detective...

00:29:08.470 --> 00:29:10.560
Mouri Kogoro.

00:29:10.560 --> 00:29:11.770
Dad.

00:29:11.770 --> 00:29:12.730
Uncle.

00:29:12.730 --> 00:29:16.150
Hey, you said that this wasn't an accident. what did you mean by that?

00:29:16.150 --> 00:29:20.820
Someone lured the sharks to attack you on purpose.

00:29:20.820 --> 00:29:26.610
They hid a bag of fish blood in the lining of this BC jacket.

00:29:20.820 --> 00:29:25.450
Note: BC is an acronym for Buoyancy control

00:29:27.870 --> 00:29:32.200
Considering you are both treasure hunters,

00:29:32.200 --> 00:29:34.540
you are the main suspects here.

00:29:37.630 --> 00:29:39.460
Hey, Ran-neechan.

00:29:40.380 --> 00:29:43.340
Where are the BC jackets usually kept?

00:29:43.340 --> 00:29:44.720
Well...

00:29:44.720 --> 00:29:47.680
We don't bring them back to the hotel room.

00:29:47.680 --> 00:29:51.010
I think they're usually kept in the diving shop,

00:29:51.010 --> 00:29:53.270
and they fill the air tanks there too.

00:30:08.570 --> 00:30:11.830
If someone wanted to tamper with the BC
 jackets, this would be the easiest place.

00:30:12.490 --> 00:30:14.910
Since it'd be risky to do anything after someone's already taken it out.

00:30:15.370 --> 00:30:16.620
Wait a second... Kudo-kun!

00:30:22.040 --> 00:30:23.300
What is it, Haibara?

00:30:24.550 --> 00:30:25.630
Look at this.

00:30:26.260 --> 00:30:29.180
They usually wash the instruments here,

00:30:29.180 --> 00:30:31.300
so this place is always damp.

00:30:31.300 --> 00:30:34.640
Thanks. Could you please take some photos for me?

00:30:34.970 --> 00:30:37.100
I have to check on other stuff.

00:30:37.100 --> 00:30:41.060
Huh? Since when did I become your assistant?

00:30:41.730 --> 00:30:44.530
Not assistant, partner!

00:30:45.650 --> 00:30:47.530
You're a smooth talker, aren't you?

00:30:47.530 --> 00:30:49.200
So, I'll be back in a bit.

00:30:49.200 --> 00:30:50.240
Yeah, yeah...

00:30:58.790 --> 00:31:00.540
Hey, Onee-san.

00:31:00.540 --> 00:31:01.670
What is it?

00:31:01.670 --> 00:31:03.960
Does anyone work here at night?

00:31:04.460 --> 00:31:06.130
Are you playing a detective game?

00:31:07.260 --> 00:31:09.380
I live behind this shop,

00:31:09.380 --> 00:31:12.050
and Kimiko lives in an apartment near the port,

00:31:12.050 --> 00:31:13.800
so there isn't anyone here at night.

00:31:13.800 --> 00:31:14.810
I see.

00:31:14.810 --> 00:31:20.440
And since there aren't any thieves on this island, we usually don't lock the door.

00:31:21.020 --> 00:31:24.360
Kimiko, you closed the shop last night, right?

00:31:24.360 --> 00:31:27.360
Y-Yeah, but why do you ask?

00:31:27.360 --> 00:31:30.700
This little detective here was asking me a few questions.

00:31:31.820 --> 00:31:33.320
I see...

00:31:33.990 --> 00:31:37.040
You're trying to figure out who could have
 done something to the BC, aren't you?

00:31:37.950 --> 00:31:43.290
It's true that I closed the shop last night and opened the shop this morning,

00:31:43.290 --> 00:31:47.500
But we don't lock the door, so anyone could have snuck in.

00:31:52.260 --> 00:31:54.010
Find anything interesting?

00:31:54.390 --> 00:31:55.350
No...

00:31:55.970 --> 00:31:58.100
Nothing of use yet.

00:31:59.060 --> 00:32:00.680
I hope you can find something.

00:32:04.060 --> 00:32:05.150
What is it?

00:32:05.150 --> 00:32:06.860
What is it?!

00:32:06.860 --> 00:32:08.690
What are you doing, Conan?

00:32:08.690 --> 00:32:12.400
We're still looking for the pirate's treasure, and can't find it without you!

00:32:12.400 --> 00:32:15.160
You need to start using your brains once in a while.

00:32:15.160 --> 00:32:17.200
We've tried, but we're completely stumped!

00:32:19.620 --> 00:32:21.460
Where are you guys right now?

00:32:21.460 --> 00:32:23.790
We're walking towards a hanging bridge.

00:32:23.790 --> 00:32:25.330
Hanging bridge?

00:32:25.330 --> 00:32:27.840
It's on the map!

00:32:27.840 --> 00:32:29.920
The treasure map...

00:32:29.920 --> 00:32:31.970
Okay, I see it.

00:32:31.970 --> 00:32:33.840
Hurry up and get over here!

00:32:33.840 --> 00:32:35.470
Okay, okay...

00:32:35.720 --> 00:32:37.300
I have no choice.

00:32:38.100 --> 00:32:40.100
Hey Haibara, you coming?

00:32:40.100 --> 00:32:41.140
I'll pass.

00:32:41.850 --> 00:32:42.980
I knew it.

00:32:44.600 --> 00:32:46.860
Hey, hey! What's this?

00:32:46.520 --> 00:32:49.190
Passage Prohibited

00:32:46.860 --> 00:32:49.360
The road is completely blocked!

00:32:49.360 --> 00:32:50.940
Geez...

00:32:52.400 --> 00:32:53.860
Are you by yourself?

00:32:54.860 --> 00:32:58.120
Your friends are over by the hanging bridge.

00:32:58.120 --> 00:32:59.990
I want to go there,

00:32:59.990 --> 00:33:02.370
but I can't use this road.

00:33:02.370 --> 00:33:03.410
Sorry, sorry,

00:33:04.000 --> 00:33:08.000
Last week, an earthquake caused a landslide which blocked the road.

00:33:08.000 --> 00:33:11.550
Up ahead, there's a road that turns left.

00:33:11.550 --> 00:33:13.130
You can use that road.

00:33:14.220 --> 00:33:15.930
Thanks, Iwanaga-san!

00:33:16.550 --> 00:33:18.390
Take care!

00:33:18.390 --> 00:33:19.300
Okay!

00:33:27.020 --> 00:33:29.980
I give up, I don't know the answer.

00:33:29.980 --> 00:33:32.440
Once Conan-kun gets here, we'll be able to solve the riddle.

00:33:32.440 --> 00:33:36.450
It's okay even if he doesn't come! Can't we still figure it out ourselves?

00:33:37.820 --> 00:33:38.740
Huh?

00:33:38.740 --> 00:33:41.330
There's a sign posted on the other side of the bridge.

00:33:43.580 --> 00:33:44.620
What does it say?

00:33:44.960 --> 00:33:46.170
Let's go take a look.

00:33:46.170 --> 00:33:46.870
Okay.

00:33:51.300 --> 00:33:53.380
I'm starving...

00:33:54.420 --> 00:33:57.470
Hey, wait for me!

00:34:12.230 --> 00:34:13.530
Wait, please!

00:34:14.070 --> 00:34:15.990
Don't move!

00:34:16.700 --> 00:34:18.570
W-Why?

00:34:19.160 --> 00:34:20.570
This is...

00:34:20.410 --> 00:34:22.410
Warning

00:34:20.410 --> 00:34:22.410
Passage 
forbidden
 to anyone
 who weighs
 over 40
 kilograms!

00:34:22.700 --> 00:34:24.580
What is it?!?

00:34:24.580 --> 00:34:26.540
How much do you weigh, Genta-kun?

00:34:26.540 --> 00:34:27.790
39 kilograms!

00:34:27.790 --> 00:34:28.460
You're lying!

00:34:30.210 --> 00:34:32.920
Wait, I might have put on a little weight recently... maybe 45 kilograms?

00:34:32.920 --> 00:34:34.250
That's really bad!

00:34:34.250 --> 00:34:38.220
The bridge will break if someone over 40 kilograms crosses it!

00:34:38.220 --> 00:34:40.180
A-Are you serious!?

00:34:40.550 --> 00:34:42.140
I see, I got it now!

00:34:42.470 --> 00:34:44.470
"A skinny pirate would just laugh."

00:34:44.470 --> 00:34:46.810
It's telling us to walk across the bridge!

00:34:46.810 --> 00:34:48.230
That's right!

00:34:48.230 --> 00:34:50.230
"A skinny pirate would just laugh" must mean...

00:34:50.230 --> 00:34:52.150
that a fat pirate would cry!

00:34:53.520 --> 00:34:56.570
Help me, Mommy!

00:34:57.440 --> 00:34:58.570
Found it!

00:35:00.820 --> 00:35:03.080
A pirate never cries.

00:35:03.370 --> 00:35:06.160
What does "a pirate never cries" mean?

00:35:06.750 --> 00:35:10.460
It's already 4 PM. Let's continue tomorrow.

00:35:11.040 --> 00:35:13.090
But how do we go back?

00:35:13.090 --> 00:35:14.210
Well...

00:35:14.630 --> 00:35:17.170
If Genta-kun keeps squatting there,

00:35:17.170 --> 00:35:20.430
The bridge will break once as soon as we step on it.

00:35:20.720 --> 00:35:23.850
Hey, what are you guys doing over there?

00:35:23.850 --> 00:35:26.270
Conan-kun, we found it!

00:35:26.270 --> 00:35:28.140
Nice going, you guys!

00:35:28.430 --> 00:35:31.560
The next hint is "a pirate never cries".

00:35:31.560 --> 00:35:36.070
However , this bridge will break if someone who weighs more than 40 kilograms goes across  it! He might fall!

00:35:36.070 --> 00:35:37.900
Was that written on that board?

00:35:37.440 --> 00:35:42.950
Warning

00:35:37.900 --> 00:35:43.120
Not really. What's written on it is "Passage forbidden to anyone who weighs over 40 kilograms!"

00:35:43.450 --> 00:35:44.830
I see.

00:35:44.830 --> 00:35:47.870
That's why the skinny pirate would laugh.

00:35:47.870 --> 00:35:50.750
It's okay, just walk through.

00:35:50.750 --> 00:35:53.040
It was just a hint.

00:35:53.040 --> 00:35:56.920
The only people who could weigh under 40 kilograms are women and children,

00:35:57.250 --> 00:36:01.970
So that was just a code that only they could solve.

00:36:27.740 --> 00:36:30.160
Thank you for coming, Inspector!

00:36:30.580 --> 00:36:33.920
But did you have to come all the way here?

00:36:34.250 --> 00:36:36.750
I found some aspects to be weird.

00:36:36.750 --> 00:36:37.960
I-Inspector!

00:36:37.960 --> 00:36:40.340
Thank you for coming all the way out here.

00:36:40.960 --> 00:36:42.720
I want to know all of the details.

00:36:43.260 --> 00:36:44.890
Yes, sir!

00:36:46.640 --> 00:36:48.890
You treat us like we're the criminals,

00:36:48.890 --> 00:36:51.680
Izu Yamataro
Treasure Hunter

00:36:49.310 --> 00:36:51.980
but we're the victims, okay?

00:36:51.980 --> 00:36:56.190
If you're the victim, then tell us the truth!

00:36:57.560 --> 00:37:01.530
Have you seen these two men?

00:37:04.280 --> 00:37:06.870
Nope. Never seen them before.

00:37:06.870 --> 00:37:11.500
They robbed a supermarket in Shinbashi last night, taking the cash from the store.

00:37:12.040 --> 00:37:14.460
They told us you ordered them to do so,

00:37:14.790 --> 00:37:17.460
as an initiation to join your gang.

00:37:17.460 --> 00:37:19.290
I don't know anything about that.

00:37:17.830 --> 00:37:20.960
Matsumoto Mitsushi
Treasure Hunter

00:37:19.290 --> 00:37:21.710
It was probably just a bluff so you incompetent police would let him go.

00:37:21.710 --> 00:37:22.880
You bastard!

00:37:22.880 --> 00:37:25.590
Do you have any evidence?

00:37:25.590 --> 00:37:27.590
Aside from their word?

00:37:29.300 --> 00:37:31.180
Now, now,

00:37:31.180 --> 00:37:33.140
Calm down, everyone.

00:37:33.140 --> 00:37:35.730
Let's have a cold drink.

00:37:51.790 --> 00:37:58.670
I'd like to return to my room if you have nothing else to say.

00:37:58.670 --> 00:38:05.090
So you have no idea who might want to attack you, Matsumoto-san?

00:38:05.090 --> 00:38:06.800
No, none at all.

00:38:07.510 --> 00:38:09.010
That's all then, I guess.

00:38:09.010 --> 00:38:12.640
Excuse me, do you happen to have a match with you?

00:38:12.640 --> 00:38:14.020
I forgot to bring my lighter with me.

00:38:14.980 --> 00:38:16.230
Here.

00:38:16.230 --> 00:38:17.390
Thanks.

00:38:25.190 --> 00:38:26.900
Thanks.

00:38:29.820 --> 00:38:32.120
What a waste of time.

00:38:35.200 --> 00:38:37.330
Can I have a sip of that?

00:38:37.330 --> 00:38:38.960
I'm a little thirsty.

00:38:38.960 --> 00:38:42.540
Go ahead. They didn't touch them at all.

00:38:42.540 --> 00:38:44.670
I was trying to get their fingerprints.

00:38:46.420 --> 00:38:48.590
But even if we had gotten their fingerprints,

00:38:48.590 --> 00:38:52.890
it takes more time,

00:38:52.890 --> 00:38:56.060
regardless of whether we got someone to come analyze them or sent them back for testing.

00:38:56.850 --> 00:38:58.730
By the way, Takagi-kun,

00:38:58.730 --> 00:39:00.060
do you smoke?

00:39:01.360 --> 00:39:02.860
Sorry.

00:39:03.440 --> 00:39:06.030
Do you have UHU glue?

00:39:13.450 --> 00:39:16.080
Sorry to interrupt your meal.

00:39:16.080 --> 00:39:17.870
Is it time for quiz?

00:39:18.750 --> 00:39:20.000
You got it.

00:39:20.000 --> 00:39:21.120
Not again...

00:39:21.120 --> 00:39:22.380
You want to play it <i>now?</i>

00:39:22.380 --> 00:39:24.590
I knew it was coming...

00:39:27.090 --> 00:39:30.630
In the fish kingdom on the abandoned ocean floor,

00:39:30.630 --> 00:39:33.300
The evil deeds of the previous king were revealed,

00:39:33.300 --> 00:39:36.180
and the sea bream fish became the next king.

00:39:36.180 --> 00:39:40.060
Of the following choices then, who was the previous king?

00:39:40.060 --> 00:39:44.150
1. Squid, 2. Octopus, or 3. Crab?

00:39:40.140 --> 00:39:44.150
Ika (Squid)

00:39:41.350 --> 00:39:44.150
Tako (Octopus)

00:39:42.770 --> 00:39:44.150
Kani (Crab)

00:39:44.310 --> 00:39:46.020
So, take a guess, guys.

00:39:50.700 --> 00:39:52.030
I know!

00:39:52.030 --> 00:39:53.410
It's the third one, the crab!

00:39:53.410 --> 00:39:54.660
Why is it the crab?

00:39:54.660 --> 00:39:57.370
It uses its pincers to cut off the heads of those it hates.

00:39:57.370 --> 00:39:59.290
What? That's so mean!

00:40:00.790 --> 00:40:01.750
Wrong, wrong.

00:40:03.080 --> 00:40:05.250
That's really far off...

00:40:07.590 --> 00:40:08.630
It must be the octopus!

00:40:09.380 --> 00:40:10.510
Why?

00:40:10.510 --> 00:40:14.930
King Octopus pocketed the kingdom's money.

00:40:14.930 --> 00:40:17.430
Just picture how an octopus looks.

00:40:18.390 --> 00:40:21.350
In other words, you're saying baldies are usually rich?

00:40:21.350 --> 00:40:22.600
That's right.

00:40:22.600 --> 00:40:23.850
I don't think so.

00:40:24.440 --> 00:40:26.360
Then, it's the first choice, the squid!

00:40:27.400 --> 00:40:28.320
Why?

00:40:29.650 --> 00:40:31.360
Let me answer that!

00:40:31.360 --> 00:40:33.610
I can do it this time.

00:40:34.950 --> 00:40:38.620
The King

00:40:34.950 --> 00:40:38.620
Osama can be separated into "o" and "sama."

00:40:38.620 --> 00:40:43.000
Squid                               King                                  Squid King

00:40:38.620 --> 00:40:43.000
Adding "ika" in front of "sama" gives you "ika-sama."

00:40:43.000 --> 00:40:45.460
Ika-sama?

00:40:45.460 --> 00:40:46.880
That means he cheated!

00:40:48.170 --> 00:40:49.670
That's right!

00:40:49.670 --> 00:40:51.800
Something's fishy here...

00:40:53.590 --> 00:40:55.760
Hey, Conan-kun!

00:40:55.590 --> 00:40:57.550
 <i>Osama</i> can be separated 
into <i>o</i> and <i>sama</i> 
adding <i>ika</i> in front of <i>sama</i>
 gives you <i>ika-sama</i>

00:40:58.350 --> 00:41:00.020
This is truly...

00:41:00.020 --> 00:41:01.060
Ikasama

00:41:00.020 --> 00:41:01.060
...Cheating.

00:41:04.600 --> 00:41:06.730
Such a beautiful moon.

00:41:06.730 --> 00:41:08.230
Yeah.

00:41:08.770 --> 00:41:12.190
By the way, I was wondering 
why you provide lodging to tourists at your house?

00:41:14.360 --> 00:41:19.080
Well, I live by myself and fish for a living.

00:41:19.740 --> 00:41:25.210
The Tourism Division asked me to provide lodging so that they could get more tourist to visit.

00:41:25.210 --> 00:41:26.750
I see...

00:41:26.750 --> 00:41:32.090
I hope that we aren't interfering with your daily life.

00:41:32.460 --> 00:41:35.930
It's better to have you stay than the treasure hunters.

00:41:36.470 --> 00:41:41.100
Speaking of treasure hunters, is there really treasure here?

00:41:42.140 --> 00:41:46.190
Hyenas don't gather at places that don't have treasure,

00:41:46.190 --> 00:41:49.900
although it's probably not the type of treasure they are expecting.

00:41:49.900 --> 00:41:51.860
I can't find the answer.

00:41:51.860 --> 00:41:54.150
Why does a pirate never cry?

00:41:54.150 --> 00:41:57.320
Genta-kun, please try to concentrate more.

00:41:57.320 --> 00:41:58.820
Hey kids...

00:41:58.820 --> 00:42:01.740
Is the hint "a pirate never cries" ?

00:42:01.740 --> 00:42:03.580
Yeah, that's right.

00:42:03.580 --> 00:42:06.500
If it's "pirates cry," I know where it is.

00:42:06.790 --> 00:42:09.790
Pirates cry?

00:42:09.790 --> 00:42:11.840
Maybe there's a hint there.

00:42:12.380 --> 00:42:14.090
Would you like to go take a look?

00:42:14.920 --> 00:42:16.470
Going out at this hour?

00:42:16.470 --> 00:42:19.390
It's dark outside. Why don't you go tomorrow?

00:42:19.390 --> 00:42:22.220
The weather might change tomorrow.

00:42:22.220 --> 00:42:23.810
Is it going to rain?

00:42:24.720 --> 00:42:28.850
We don't go out to the sea when the south wind starts blowing.

00:42:28.850 --> 00:42:30.730
The waves will be very violent, almost like a storm.

00:42:30.730 --> 00:42:32.770
Is that called "Life Knowledge"?

00:42:33.150 --> 00:42:34.900
Then, let's go together.

00:42:34.900 --> 00:42:36.700
It can be an after-dinner walk.

00:42:36.700 --> 00:42:37.650
Yay!

00:42:42.830 --> 00:42:45.250
What are you trying to do, Takagi-kun?

00:42:46.250 --> 00:42:49.670
This is called cyanide methacrylate.

00:42:49.670 --> 00:42:54.380
UHU glue contains cyanide methacrylate,

00:42:54.380 --> 00:42:58.010
which reacts to the water in secretion.

00:42:58.010 --> 00:43:00.720
You can use this to get fingerprints.

00:43:01.180 --> 00:43:04.890
Now you just have to wait for the fingerprints to show.

00:43:05.770 --> 00:43:08.100
You're really talented to know how to do this!

00:43:09.230 --> 00:43:11.690
Actually... I saw this method in a movie one time,

00:43:11.690 --> 00:43:14.360
so I asked an officer from the identification bureau how to do it.

00:43:14.360 --> 00:43:17.320
Then, I hope this works as smoothly as it did in the movie.

00:43:28.960 --> 00:43:32.710
Hey, is this where the "a pirate never cries" hint leads to?

00:43:32.710 --> 00:43:36.210
I don't know if this is the right place, but the "cry" place is here.

00:43:37.170 --> 00:43:38.260
Cry...

00:43:38.970 --> 00:43:40.840
Is it the sound of the wind...?

00:43:40.840 --> 00:43:42.640
It kind of sounds like someone crying...

00:43:43.140 --> 00:43:44.220
It really does!

00:43:44.220 --> 00:43:46.970
Except that I heard the wind on the way here as well.

00:43:47.770 --> 00:43:49.730
Well, I knew that already!

00:43:52.270 --> 00:43:56.190
The sand here contains a lot of quartz,

00:43:56.520 --> 00:43:58.070
and it's fine too.

00:44:04.620 --> 00:44:06.030
I see.

00:44:08.290 --> 00:44:09.700
Hey, Conan...

00:44:09.700 --> 00:44:11.120
What did you find out?

00:44:12.170 --> 00:44:13.580
Listen carefully.

00:44:16.460 --> 00:44:18.050
The <i>sand</i> is crying!

00:44:18.050 --> 00:44:21.970
So that's why it was "a <i>pirate</i> never cries"!

00:44:21.970 --> 00:44:24.430
You'll have to figure out the rest yourselves.

00:44:24.430 --> 00:44:25.930
Okay.

00:44:26.350 --> 00:44:29.810
The hint is "a pirate never cries".

00:44:31.390 --> 00:44:32.560
Could it be there?

00:44:36.940 --> 00:44:39.030
Come over here! There's no sound here.

00:44:39.030 --> 00:44:42.110
So that's the "a pirate never cries" place!

00:44:48.280 --> 00:44:50.540
They sure set this up to create the right atmosphere...

00:44:53.040 --> 00:44:54.960
A pirate's soul will 
go to heaven

00:44:55.250 --> 00:44:59.590
The next one is, "A pirate's soul will go to heaven".

00:44:59.590 --> 00:45:01.510
Another odd hint again.

00:45:01.800 --> 00:45:05.430
The head of the Tourism Division sure is good!

00:45:05.890 --> 00:45:08.350
Iwanaga-san, the head of the Tourism Division.

00:45:08.350 --> 00:45:11.930
He said that he thought of these riddles himself.

00:45:12.980 --> 00:45:15.900
That's his job after all.

00:45:16.860 --> 00:45:18.860
Such an impassive person...

00:45:20.940 --> 00:45:22.030
What is it?

00:45:24.570 --> 00:45:26.110
What is it, Conan-kun?

00:45:29.280 --> 00:45:31.120
This is getting interesting.

00:45:31.700 --> 00:45:32.870
Conan-kun?

00:45:33.870 --> 00:45:36.710
Sorry, I need to go somewhere for a bit.

00:45:36.710 --> 00:45:37.790
Why don't you all head back without me?

00:45:37.790 --> 00:45:39.540
Wait, Conan-kun!

00:45:39.540 --> 00:45:40.670
Not again...

00:45:41.300 --> 00:45:43.720
That brat has no team spirit at all.

00:45:43.720 --> 00:45:44.970
Conan-kun...

00:45:57.020 --> 00:45:58.150
It appeared!

00:45:58.730 --> 00:46:02.690
Now we just have to change it into data and send it on to be examined.

00:46:02.690 --> 00:46:04.030
Well done Takagi-kun!

00:46:04.030 --> 00:46:05.320
It was nothing...

00:46:06.490 --> 00:46:09.620
Tell me if you ever want to transfer to the Identification bureau.

00:46:10.070 --> 00:46:13.120
I can write you a recommendation letter.

00:46:13.120 --> 00:46:14.750
Please don't joke with me.

00:46:15.620 --> 00:46:17.790
Anyway, send that back to headquarters.

00:46:17.790 --> 00:46:19.040
Right away!

00:46:53.450 --> 00:46:55.250
What are you doing here?

00:46:55.250 --> 00:46:58.830
I was taking a walk and I got lost.

00:46:59.290 --> 00:47:00.830
How do I get back to Koumi Inn?

00:47:01.420 --> 00:47:02.290
Go that way.

00:47:02.670 --> 00:47:05.170
Thank you. Good night!

00:47:10.050 --> 00:47:11.970
How is it, Takagi-kun?

00:47:11.970 --> 00:47:13.640
Any news from headquarters yet?

00:47:13.640 --> 00:47:15.220
Nope, not yet.

00:47:15.640 --> 00:47:17.180
I see.

00:47:20.270 --> 00:47:21.060
What's wrong?!

00:47:23.230 --> 00:47:25.690
Tourism Division

00:47:23.940 --> 00:47:25.820
The alarm in the Tourism Division has gone off!

00:47:31.410 --> 00:47:34.740
Then, something must have happened in the Tourism Division's office.

00:47:34.740 --> 00:47:37.500
No, their alarm often malfunctions.

00:47:37.500 --> 00:47:39.620
We better go and take a look just in case.

00:47:39.620 --> 00:47:40.670
Where is it?

00:47:40.670 --> 00:47:42.880
Next to the police station.

00:47:42.880 --> 00:47:44.040
We'll be borrowing your car...

00:47:44.040 --> 00:47:45.000
Okay.

00:47:45.000 --> 00:47:47.510
Headquarters might send a report back later.

00:47:47.510 --> 00:47:48.260
Please take care of it.

00:47:48.670 --> 00:47:50.430
G-Got it.

00:48:05.110 --> 00:48:08.780
Damn, why are there so many incidents happening lately?

00:48:09.360 --> 00:48:11.030
I-It's here!

00:48:12.990 --> 00:48:13.910
Let's see...

00:48:20.250 --> 00:48:21.960
Th-This is...

00:48:49.650 --> 00:48:50.990
Hurry, get in!

00:49:40.740 --> 00:49:47.880
Geez, I asked for about pubs with beautiful hostesses.

00:49:53.210 --> 00:49:54.130
Damn...

00:49:54.130 --> 00:49:56.340
Can't I have a drink in peace?

00:49:56.340 --> 00:49:58.550
I hate coming to tourist spots.

00:49:58.550 --> 00:50:00.180
I'm getting angry!

00:50:01.260 --> 00:50:03.140
Hey, shut up!

00:50:03.140 --> 00:50:04.730
Huh? What happened?

00:50:06.140 --> 00:50:07.560
Hey, wait a minute!

00:50:08.520 --> 00:50:10.190
What are you doing?

00:50:11.320 --> 00:50:15.860
There aren't any beautiful hostesses here, Head of the Tourism Division!

00:50:15.860 --> 00:50:17.490
What does it matter?

00:50:17.490 --> 00:50:20.030
She'll look beautiful when she's in a dark room anyway!

00:50:20.030 --> 00:50:21.490
You have to take responsibility!

00:50:21.490 --> 00:50:23.160
I'm busy right now!

00:50:23.160 --> 00:50:24.040
What?!

00:50:24.040 --> 00:50:27.460
Someone broke into the display room at the Tourism Division's office.

00:50:27.460 --> 00:50:29.670
What? A thief?

00:50:29.670 --> 00:50:31.130
Let me take the bike.

00:50:31.460 --> 00:50:32.880
Wait a minute.

00:50:32.880 --> 00:50:36.170
Get on! Or I'll go without you!

00:50:36.170 --> 00:50:37.970
Please wait for me!

00:50:37.970 --> 00:50:40.220
Sit tight, I'm going to go fast!

00:50:40.220 --> 00:50:42.850
Wait, you haven't paid your bill yet!

00:50:42.850 --> 00:50:45.020
Customer-san!

00:50:45.640 --> 00:50:47.440
What's the problem, ma'am?

00:50:47.440 --> 00:50:49.440
Uehira-chan, someone ran away and didn't pay his bill.

00:50:49.440 --> 00:50:50.690
Please get him for me.

00:50:51.020 --> 00:50:54.110
Geez... Not <i>another</i> incident!

00:50:55.900 --> 00:50:58.950
They broke the display counter using a small crowbar.

00:50:59.320 --> 00:51:00.700
It was a pretty bold move.

00:51:05.580 --> 00:51:07.080
Yes, Sato-kun?

00:51:08.000 --> 00:51:10.960
Like Conan-kun said, there were gunshots.

00:51:10.960 --> 00:51:12.670
There are blood stains at the crime scene.

00:51:12.670 --> 00:51:13.880
I see.

00:51:14.500 --> 00:51:16.170
Can you maintain the area?

00:51:16.630 --> 00:51:18.670
It would be quiet difficult to do so.

00:51:18.670 --> 00:51:19.970
That's what I was afraid of.

00:51:19.970 --> 00:51:23.600
Take a picture of the crime scene and come back here.

00:51:23.600 --> 00:51:24.430
Yes, sir!

00:51:28.810 --> 00:51:30.390
The cutlass and the pistol were stolen!

00:51:31.150 --> 00:51:33.060
Were they worth a lot?

00:51:33.060 --> 00:51:35.730
They were priceless artifacts found inside Seabed Palace,

00:51:36.280 --> 00:51:40.150
the cutlass of Anne Bonny and the pistol of Mary Read.

00:51:40.150 --> 00:51:43.530
There's no need to worry, cause I'm here!

00:51:44.740 --> 00:51:46.990
Mouri-kun, you're red.

00:51:47.410 --> 00:51:48.830
No,

00:51:48.830 --> 00:51:50.960
I'm just excited to see everyone here.

00:51:50.960 --> 00:51:53.670
Mouri Kogoro, you are under arrest!

00:51:53.670 --> 00:51:57.590
You didn't pay your bill, stole a bicycle, and were riding it while drunk!

00:52:02.970 --> 00:52:04.220
Hey, hey...

00:52:04.930 --> 00:52:06.930
Is that true?

00:52:06.930 --> 00:52:07.770
Yes.

00:52:07.770 --> 00:52:10.020
He didn't pay his bill at the pub,

00:52:10.020 --> 00:52:12.730
stole Iwanaga-san's bicycle, and rode away.

00:52:12.730 --> 00:52:13.900
That's what the hostess told me.

00:52:13.900 --> 00:52:15.650
I didn't steal his bike.

00:52:15.650 --> 00:52:19.030
I rode him here while he sat right behind me!

00:52:19.030 --> 00:52:19.940
Right? Right?

00:52:19.940 --> 00:52:20.950
Yeah...

00:52:22.450 --> 00:52:24.910
Oh! I almost forgot, Inspector...

00:52:24.910 --> 00:52:27.200
The results from the fingerprints analysis arrived.

00:52:28.410 --> 00:52:31.250
Hey, is this true?

00:52:32.170 --> 00:52:33.920
Matsumoto Mitsushi.

00:52:33.920 --> 00:52:36.290
He has stolen important cultural artifacts from ruins all over the world,

00:52:36.290 --> 00:52:39.800
along with committing theft and burglary of works of art, and even murder.

00:52:39.800 --> 00:52:40.800
He's a big fish.

00:52:40.800 --> 00:52:44.390
So they're international fugitives.

00:52:44.390 --> 00:52:48.390
Damn, so they really are trying to steal Anne and Mary's treasure.

00:52:49.100 --> 00:52:50.470
What do you mean?

00:52:50.810 --> 00:52:54.730
There's more treasure besides the stolen cutlass and pistol?

00:52:55.190 --> 00:52:56.400
Yes.

00:52:56.400 --> 00:52:59.780
Anne Bonny and Mary Read were pirates.

00:53:00.360 --> 00:53:03.150
Before they got caught 300 years ago,

00:53:03.530 --> 00:53:07.120
they hid their treasure here in Koumi Island.

00:53:08.080 --> 00:53:10.660
Is it true that they hid their treasure here?

00:53:10.660 --> 00:53:14.790
Yes, the stolen pistol and cutlass are the best evidence of that.

00:53:22.590 --> 00:53:24.130
Hey, Uncle...

00:53:24.130 --> 00:53:26.840
I thought you were at a pub with beautiful hostesses.

00:53:29.140 --> 00:53:31.600
Not only was she not beautiful,

00:53:31.600 --> 00:53:34.060
she was an old hag!

00:53:34.060 --> 00:53:35.440
I knew it.

00:53:35.440 --> 00:53:37.060
It's that smell.

00:53:39.520 --> 00:53:41.570
You've got something on you, Uncle.

00:53:41.570 --> 00:53:43.990
What is this?

00:53:44.780 --> 00:53:46.320
I see.

00:53:48.320 --> 00:53:50.700
How do you get off of this island?

00:53:50.700 --> 00:53:53.870
There is only one scheduled ship that leaves here every afternoon,

00:53:53.870 --> 00:53:55.870
but you could also leave in a fishing boat.

00:53:55.870 --> 00:53:59.170
Alright then, ask everyone to be extra careful,

00:53:59.170 --> 00:54:00.880
to avoid having their fishing boats stolen.

00:54:00.880 --> 00:54:02.590
Understood!

00:54:03.300 --> 00:54:05.340
Hey, what about the cuffs?

00:54:05.340 --> 00:54:06.880
Hey!!

00:54:06.880 --> 00:54:08.800
Hey, Inspector Megure...

00:54:09.390 --> 00:54:16.940
I saw that Matsumoto guy paying on the diving shop owner, Mabuchi-san.

00:54:16.940 --> 00:54:17.850
What?

00:54:17.850 --> 00:54:18.810
Inspector Megure,

00:54:19.440 --> 00:54:21.070
we're back.

00:54:21.070 --> 00:54:22.150
Thank you for your hard work.

00:54:22.150 --> 00:54:23.530
I need you to check on something.

00:54:23.530 --> 00:54:27.070
The diving shop owner has had some contact with Matsumoto.

00:54:27.070 --> 00:54:29.240
Both of you immediately go to the diving shop.

00:54:29.620 --> 00:54:32.030
We'll go to the hotel where Matsumoto is staying.

00:54:32.030 --> 00:54:32.830
Yes, sir!

00:54:32.830 --> 00:54:35.000
Inspector Megure, the cuffs on my wrists!

00:54:48.380 --> 00:54:50.010
How's the weather?

00:54:50.010 --> 00:54:51.850
The wind is strong...

00:54:52.260 --> 00:54:54.770
but since the sun is out, there shouldn't be a problem.

00:54:55.980 --> 00:54:57.480
I'll zoom in on the picture.

00:55:00.400 --> 00:55:02.360
The pattern on the tracks is different from the ones on the tire.

00:55:03.360 --> 00:55:05.820
Just like I thought, it's not this bike.

00:55:05.820 --> 00:55:07.070
Conan-kun?

00:55:07.490 --> 00:55:08.740
Yeah?

00:55:09.570 --> 00:55:11.700
Conan-kun, the food is ready!

00:55:11.700 --> 00:55:12.910
Be there in a second!

00:55:13.580 --> 00:55:14.410
What is it?

00:55:15.160 --> 00:55:16.910
I think it's a GPS tracker.

00:55:16.910 --> 00:55:20.580
GPS tracker? Why would a bike have one of those?

00:55:23.040 --> 00:55:25.500
Geez... What is Conan doing?

00:55:25.500 --> 00:55:28.170
He said he was coming, just give him a minute!

00:55:28.170 --> 00:55:28.800
Here he comes!

00:55:28.800 --> 00:55:29.680
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:55:29.680 --> 00:55:32.550
You are so slow, Conan. I'm starving!

00:55:32.550 --> 00:55:33.930
Sorry, sorry.

00:55:34.890 --> 00:55:37.520
Huh? Where's Uncle?

00:55:38.230 --> 00:55:41.730
He has a meeting with the police, so he went down to the station.

00:55:42.980 --> 00:55:44.730
Okay then, everyone's here.

00:55:44.730 --> 00:55:46.530
Let's dig in!

00:55:48.990 --> 00:55:51.450
I never thought that it'd be nearby!

00:56:00.250 --> 00:56:01.960
Yummy! I want another one!

00:56:01.960 --> 00:56:05.710
Hey, did you meet Iwanaga-san on the way to the hanging bridge?

00:56:05.710 --> 00:56:07.250
Iwanaga-san?

00:56:07.630 --> 00:56:09.470
Ah, you mean the head of the Tourism Division?

00:56:09.470 --> 00:56:10.550
Yeah.

00:56:10.550 --> 00:56:13.340
No, we didn't see him, right?

00:56:13.340 --> 00:56:14.470
Yep.

00:56:14.470 --> 00:56:17.260
We found that place ourselves.

00:56:17.560 --> 00:56:18.770
I see.

00:56:22.770 --> 00:56:24.610
Does everyone have enough food?

00:56:25.310 --> 00:56:28.110
Yes, we're fine. Thank you very much.

00:56:29.280 --> 00:56:31.700
Are you going for a dive today as well?

00:56:31.700 --> 00:56:35.370
No, my heart is still fluttering with fear from what happened yesterday.

00:56:35.370 --> 00:56:38.580
But there won't be any time left tomorrow,

00:56:38.580 --> 00:56:40.960
so we'd like to take a boat ride later.

00:56:40.960 --> 00:56:43.500
Better not go out to sea this afternoon,

00:56:44.080 --> 00:56:45.580
The waves might get stormy.

00:56:45.960 --> 00:56:47.800
Really?

00:56:48.170 --> 00:56:51.130
Then, we need to hurry up and find the treasure before that happens.

00:56:51.420 --> 00:56:55.050
You're right, we only have one hint left now.

00:56:55.050 --> 00:56:57.050
Let's work together, Conan-kun.

00:56:57.850 --> 00:57:01.980
I need to go somewhere, so you guys go ahead without me!

00:57:05.310 --> 00:57:09.650
Well, I guess we'll leave the anti-social guy here.

00:57:09.650 --> 00:57:13.280
Let's find the treasure and split it amongst ourselves.

00:57:13.280 --> 00:57:14.820
Sounds good to me!

00:57:25.790 --> 00:57:28.840
I thought so. None of the other bikes have GPS trackers.

00:57:28.840 --> 00:57:31.670
Sir, the latest information on the weather.

00:57:33.380 --> 00:57:36.640
That's not good... it looks like a small typhoon.

00:57:36.640 --> 00:57:39.810
Anyway, go and let the fishing association and the hotel know.

00:57:39.810 --> 00:57:40.640
Yes.

00:57:40.640 --> 00:57:41.930
What a pain...

00:57:51.980 --> 00:57:55.200
Matsumoto and Izuyama haven't gone back to their hotel room yet,

00:57:55.200 --> 00:57:57.740
but there's nothing that shows that they left the island either.

00:57:58.120 --> 00:58:00.700
So, they must be hiding somewhere.

00:58:00.990 --> 00:58:07.920
At least one of them was shot. They're probably looking for a doctor.

00:58:07.920 --> 00:58:11.380
I've checked with the clinics, but there's no sign of them.

00:58:11.800 --> 00:58:14.920
About the diving shop owner, Mabuchi,

00:58:14.920 --> 00:58:17.130
I found out what Conan-kun saw last night.

00:58:17.430 --> 00:58:20.470
Matsumoto was asking her to prepare a boat for them to escape in.

00:58:21.260 --> 00:58:23.060
First of all...

00:58:23.060 --> 00:58:25.810
Let me tell you that I have no idea where Matsumoto is.

00:58:26.140 --> 00:58:29.650
It's hard to make a living from just this diving shop,

00:58:29.650 --> 00:58:31.980
so I agreed to help Matsumoto.

00:58:32.610 --> 00:58:34.610
I never thought that I'd have such bad luck.

00:58:35.360 --> 00:58:36.610
I see.

00:58:36.610 --> 00:58:40.320
The bullet shells that Takagi-kun found were from old bullets,

00:58:40.320 --> 00:58:44.830
Bullets that had been stored and preserved for a very long time.

00:58:45.660 --> 00:58:49.580
We're checking with the hunter's association in regards to the rifle.

00:58:50.670 --> 00:58:51.630
Please come in.

00:58:52.210 --> 00:58:54.000
Sorry to interrupt,

00:58:54.000 --> 00:58:59.550
but I just got a report saying that Mineo-san, a member of the hunter's association, is missing his rifle.

00:58:59.550 --> 00:59:01.100
Is that so?

00:59:01.100 --> 00:59:02.930
Who is Mineo-san?

00:59:03.640 --> 00:59:06.390
He's an old man living all by himself.

00:59:06.390 --> 00:59:11.770
His niece, Mabuchi Chika-san who runs the diving shop, takes care of him.

00:59:14.360 --> 00:59:17.320
Ask Mineo-san for more details,

00:59:17.320 --> 00:59:20.280
and please ask Mabuchi-san to come over here as well.

00:59:20.280 --> 00:59:21.410
Yes, Sir!

00:59:23.580 --> 00:59:26.620
Do your best to find the stolen cutlass and pistol!

00:59:26.910 --> 00:59:28.160
I'm begging you!

00:59:28.790 --> 00:59:30.460
We'll do our best.

00:59:31.040 --> 00:59:35.050
But, why did they wait until now...

00:59:35.050 --> 00:59:37.090
Why commit the crime while all of the police are here?

00:59:37.090 --> 00:59:41.430
That's true. When Uehira-san was the only officer here,

00:59:41.430 --> 00:59:44.220
it would have been much easier to get off of the island.

00:59:44.220 --> 00:59:49.390
Most likely, the criminal was worried that his identity might be exposed if this went on.

00:59:49.390 --> 00:59:52.310
What about the backup from Tokyo?

00:59:52.900 --> 00:59:56.610
Helicopters can't come because of the low air pressure from the storm, and ships would take too long.

00:59:58.030 --> 01:00:00.360
We have to depend on ourselves...

01:00:00.360 --> 01:00:02.700
Not only in looking for Matsumoto,

01:00:03.030 --> 01:00:06.950
but also the person who attempted to kill them.

01:00:15.630 --> 01:00:16.550
There it is...

01:00:18.420 --> 01:00:19.670
I found it!

01:00:19.670 --> 01:00:21.180
Great!

01:00:21.180 --> 01:00:23.470
The last hint was really easy!

01:00:24.010 --> 01:00:27.060
"A pirate's soul will go to heaven."

01:00:27.060 --> 01:00:28.850
The only possibility is the observatory!

01:00:31.310 --> 01:00:37.520
The numbers on the stamps are the hint.

01:00:31.770 --> 01:00:34.230
"The numbers on the stamps are the hint."

01:00:34.230 --> 01:00:36.900
"Now, go find our treasure!"

01:00:37.860 --> 01:00:40.860
My boss went to go check on the situation at sea.

01:00:40.860 --> 01:00:42.240
Please wait for just a moment.

01:00:42.240 --> 01:00:43.160
Okay.

01:00:43.160 --> 01:00:44.740
Sorry to keep you waiting.

01:00:44.740 --> 01:00:49.040
Sorry! I don't think we can go out to sea today.

01:00:49.040 --> 01:00:50.750
The waves are really rough out there.

01:00:50.750 --> 01:00:52.160
How unlucky...

01:00:52.160 --> 01:00:53.710
But nothing can be done.

01:00:53.710 --> 01:00:57.250
Let's just go to a beach then.

01:00:58.340 --> 01:01:00.300
Good morning, Uehira-san.

01:01:00.710 --> 01:01:01.630
Good morning.

01:01:01.630 --> 01:01:03.550
Why do you look so serious?

01:01:03.550 --> 01:01:04.760
Did something happen?

01:01:05.260 --> 01:01:07.720
Chika-chan, please come with me.

01:01:08.220 --> 01:01:10.680
Inspector Megure would like to talk to you.

01:01:19.570 --> 01:01:20.730
Uncle!

01:01:21.280 --> 01:01:22.490
What is it?

01:01:24.110 --> 01:01:30.910
Why did the treasure hunters steal the cutlass and pistol from the Tourism Division?

01:01:33.330 --> 01:01:35.120
They, should be after The treasure...

01:01:35.120 --> 01:01:37.380
But instead stole those items.

01:01:38.090 --> 01:01:44.760
Could it be that they need them to get to the real treasure?

01:01:45.340 --> 01:01:50.220
That's why I think those men went to where the treasure is hidden.

01:01:51.180 --> 01:01:52.680
Uncle, do you know where it is?

01:01:54.270 --> 01:01:57.150
Why are you asking me?

01:01:57.150 --> 01:01:58.860
Uncle, did you used to be...

01:01:59.480 --> 01:02:01.610
...a treasure hunter too?

01:02:08.660 --> 01:02:12.540
Even if I were a treasure hunter,

01:02:12.540 --> 01:02:16.250
How would I know where the treasure is hidden?

01:02:16.830 --> 01:02:19.210
Didn't you say it yesterday?

01:02:19.590 --> 01:02:24.510
Speaking of treasure hunters, is there really treasure here?

01:02:24.510 --> 01:02:29.260
Hmph, hyenas don't gather at places that don't have treasure,

01:02:29.260 --> 01:02:32.510
although it's probably not the type of treasure they are expecting.

01:02:33.640 --> 01:02:37.310
"It's probably not the type of treasure they are expecting."

01:02:37.900 --> 01:02:41.440
So, you know what the treasure is, right?

01:02:45.900 --> 01:02:47.070
Follow me.

01:02:54.330 --> 01:02:58.420
Why are some of the numbers red, and some blue?

01:03:00.630 --> 01:03:01.920
Give me a pair of scissors.

01:03:01.920 --> 01:03:03.210
Okay.

01:03:06.260 --> 01:03:08.380
There are two questions:

01:03:08.380 --> 01:03:11.390
Why are they separated into two colors?

01:03:11.390 --> 01:03:13.510
And what do the numbers mean?

01:03:13.510 --> 01:03:16.980
Could the numbers lead to an address on this island?

01:03:18.560 --> 01:03:19.980
I know!

01:03:19.980 --> 01:03:21.770
Let's ask Uncle!

01:03:21.770 --> 01:03:23.150
Uncle!

01:03:30.860 --> 01:03:35.490
I wonder what Inspector Megure needs Mabuchi-san for?

01:03:35.490 --> 01:03:37.200
Maybe it's related to the case...

01:03:37.660 --> 01:03:39.540
There's probably just some kind of misunderstanding.

01:03:39.540 --> 01:03:40.830
Hop in, you two.

01:03:40.830 --> 01:03:41.880
Okay!

01:03:48.880 --> 01:03:51.720
Put these in the car as well.

01:03:51.720 --> 01:03:52.970
Wait, you?!

01:03:54.390 --> 01:03:56.180
Get back in the car!

01:03:56.720 --> 01:03:58.730
You wouldn't want anything to happen to your friend here...

01:04:25.460 --> 01:04:28.380
Uncle, did you used to be a treasure hunter?

01:04:28.380 --> 01:04:31.380
Yes, when I was young.

01:04:31.380 --> 01:04:37.640
I came to this island to look for the treasure of Anne and Mary, and I've been here ever since.

01:04:37.640 --> 01:04:42.020
That was when I fell in love with a woman,
 married her, and became a fisherman.

01:04:43.810 --> 01:04:45.940
This is a map of how this island looked 300 years ago.

01:05:02.080 --> 01:05:03.830
And that's how it is...

01:05:05.290 --> 01:05:07.290
The numbers are drawn according to this map.

01:05:07.750 --> 01:05:10.170
Iwanaga-san, from the Tourism Division...

01:05:10.170 --> 01:05:13.430
He wrote those numbers out according to this ancient map.

01:05:13.430 --> 01:05:16.680
But, so far, no one's been able to piece the puzzle together.

01:05:17.350 --> 01:05:20.390
So, it was created 300 years ago,

01:05:20.390 --> 01:05:22.850
by Anne Bonny herself.

01:05:23.390 --> 01:05:24.440
Yes.

01:05:24.440 --> 01:05:26.310
So we will find the real treasure

01:05:26.310 --> 01:05:28.770
If we manage to solve the riddle?

01:05:29.360 --> 01:05:31.110
Probably.

01:05:32.860 --> 01:05:36.950
There were no addresses here 300 years ago.

01:05:36.950 --> 01:05:40.040
The easiest way to solve this code would be to use the alphabet.

01:05:40.040 --> 01:05:42.040
So, the number five means...

01:05:42.080 --> 01:05:42.910
Five means...

01:05:43.000 --> 01:05:44.670
A, B, C, D, E...

01:05:44.670 --> 01:05:45.080
It's "E"!

01:05:45.080 --> 01:05:45.540
That's right!

01:05:48.920 --> 01:05:50.500
Seven is "G"!

01:05:50.500 --> 01:05:51.420
12 is...

01:05:51.420 --> 01:05:51.630
A,

01:05:51.630 --> 01:05:51.840
A, B,

01:05:51.840 --> 01:05:52.130
A, B, C,

01:05:52.130 --> 01:05:52.420
A, B, C, D,

01:05:52.420 --> 01:05:52.670
A, B, C, D, E,

01:05:52.670 --> 01:05:52.880
A, B, C, D, E, F,

01:05:52.880 --> 01:05:53.170
A, B, C, D, E, F, G,

01:05:53.170 --> 01:05:53.510
A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H,

01:05:53.510 --> 01:05:53.760
A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H, I,

01:05:53.760 --> 01:05:54.090
A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H, I, J,

01:05:54.090 --> 01:05:54.300
A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H, I, J, K,

01:05:54.300 --> 01:05:55.590
A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H, I, J, K, um...

01:05:56.050 --> 01:05:57.720
The 12th letter is "L".

01:05:57.720 --> 01:05:58.390
It's "L"!

01:06:12.400 --> 01:06:14.240
These are all the letters.

01:06:14.240 --> 01:06:15.820
The red letters are on top,

01:06:15.820 --> 01:06:19.490
and the blue letters are on the bottom.

01:06:19.490 --> 01:06:21.660
Now, we just have to unscramble them.

01:06:21.660 --> 01:06:23.120
Is it a name?

01:06:23.120 --> 01:06:25.540
Red could be their last name, and blue could be their first name.

01:06:26.080 --> 01:06:27.290
That's possible.

01:06:29.380 --> 01:06:32.090
Do you think it's related to the two pirates?

01:06:32.550 --> 01:06:34.210
Probably.

01:06:34.210 --> 01:06:37.680
Look, look! This looks like a name!

01:06:40.720 --> 01:06:42.680
It's... "Jolly"?

01:06:43.720 --> 01:06:44.890
"Jolly..."?

01:06:58.280 --> 01:06:59.570
Girls, hurry and escape!

01:07:05.410 --> 01:07:06.620
Don't move!

01:07:08.420 --> 01:07:09.620
Ran!

01:07:09.960 --> 01:07:13.340
So, you know karate, miss?

01:07:13.340 --> 01:07:16.420
But, if you don't listen to me, your friend's going to die.

01:07:36.150 --> 01:07:37.740
This is our boat...

01:07:38.400 --> 01:07:40.410
Why is it here?

01:07:40.410 --> 01:07:42.950
I asked your boss, the owner, to prepare it for me.

01:07:43.830 --> 01:07:45.580
Money talks, doesn't it...?

01:07:45.580 --> 01:07:47.700
N-No way...

01:07:47.700 --> 01:07:49.160
You're of no use to me anymore.

01:07:52.130 --> 01:07:54.040
We don't have enough air tanks.

01:07:54.040 --> 01:07:55.130
Kimiko-san!

01:07:55.130 --> 01:07:56.210
Don't move!

01:07:56.210 --> 01:07:57.630
Bitch, stop moving!

01:07:59.090 --> 01:08:00.930
Come on, come on! Get on the boat!

01:08:04.760 --> 01:08:08.310
Why do I such at this...

01:08:08.310 --> 01:08:09.980
Well, how about this?

01:08:09.980 --> 01:08:11.770
How do you read that?

01:08:12.060 --> 01:08:13.610
I think it's pronounced "Groe"...

01:08:14.190 --> 01:08:15.570
Is it "Jolly Groe"?

01:08:15.570 --> 01:08:16.440
No...

01:08:21.530 --> 01:08:22.660
It's "Roger".

01:08:23.160 --> 01:08:24.570
"Jolly Roger!"

01:08:25.780 --> 01:08:27.240
"Jolly Roger?"

01:08:27.240 --> 01:08:28.290
Who is that?

01:08:28.290 --> 01:08:29.830
Is that a famous pirate or something?

01:08:30.580 --> 01:08:33.500
The direct translation would be "Happy Roger", right?

01:08:34.080 --> 01:08:36.040
"Jolly Roger"...

01:08:36.040 --> 01:08:40.630
It's something that sailors in the 17th century never wanted to see.

01:08:41.170 --> 01:08:45.850
The name consist of "Jolly Rouge", which means "Red Flag",

01:08:45.850 --> 01:08:48.810
and "Old Roger", which means "Demon".

01:08:49.100 --> 01:08:50.060
"Red Flag?"

01:08:50.060 --> 01:08:51.230
"Demon?"

01:08:52.980 --> 01:08:54.270
Yes,

01:08:54.270 --> 01:08:57.270
The "Jolly Roger" the puzzle is referring to...

01:08:57.270 --> 01:08:59.230
is the pirate flag on the map.

01:08:59.230 --> 01:09:01.530
Amazing, Conan-kun!

01:09:03.780 --> 01:09:04.870
Well done.

01:09:08.120 --> 01:09:09.200
What's this?

01:09:09.200 --> 01:09:16.670
300 years ago, a sailor drew this as they were passing through on a ship bound for Spain.

01:09:17.290 --> 01:09:20.800
This island has since sunk into the sea.

01:09:20.800 --> 01:09:24.010
I heard it was due to methane hydrate.

01:09:27.010 --> 01:09:32.270
Yorioya Island used to be exposed above water.

01:09:29.510 --> 01:09:34.900
Koumi Island

01:09:29.510 --> 01:09:34.900
Yorioya Island

01:09:32.270 --> 01:09:37.360
Three hundred years ago, earthquakes caused it to sink into the ocean depths.

01:09:45.820 --> 01:09:47.620
Yorioya Island?

01:09:47.620 --> 01:09:49.410
Does that mean there's treasure on that island?

01:09:49.410 --> 01:09:51.290
Yeah, most likely.

01:09:51.870 --> 01:09:54.000
But there must be something else,

01:09:54.000 --> 01:09:57.710
something that gives a better hint.

01:09:58.880 --> 01:10:00.420
What is it, Conan?

01:10:00.420 --> 01:10:02.090
Did you find something?

01:10:02.090 --> 01:10:05.010
This pirate flag drawn on the ancient map...

01:10:06.050 --> 01:10:07.720
The skull's teeth...

01:10:08.050 --> 01:10:10.010
... don't you think they look like letters?

01:10:13.850 --> 01:10:15.440
You're right,

01:10:15.440 --> 01:10:17.150
They look like letters from the alphabet!

01:10:17.900 --> 01:10:21.230
The top row is D-O-S.

01:10:21.230 --> 01:10:26.320
The bottom row is D-I-O-S-A-S.

01:10:27.030 --> 01:10:28.780
What does it mean?

01:10:28.780 --> 01:10:30.030
It says "Dos Diosas".

01:10:30.580 --> 01:10:35.250
Two goddesses

01:10:31.080 --> 01:10:34.540
It means "Two goddesses in Spanish".

01:10:35.250 --> 01:10:36.540
Amazing!

01:10:36.870 --> 01:10:38.580
As expected of you, Haibara-san!

01:10:39.000 --> 01:10:40.880
So, is that it?

01:10:40.880 --> 01:10:43.050
We should go to the island to take a look.

01:10:43.050 --> 01:10:47.050
But, aren't the treasure hunters looking for treasure in the ocean?

01:10:47.050 --> 01:10:49.430
So, that must mean the treasure is underwater.

01:10:49.430 --> 01:10:54.310
No, there would have been a hint about the ocean
 if it was really underwater.

01:10:54.310 --> 01:10:57.270
Not to mention, Poseidon is the <i>male</i> god of the sea.

01:10:57.600 --> 01:11:01.060
They're probably looking for another way to get in.

01:11:02.610 --> 01:11:06.900
The entrance of the two goddesses collapsed because of the landslide,

01:11:07.150 --> 01:11:10.160
and no adult can pass through.

01:11:10.870 --> 01:11:12.870
So they must have found another entrance somewhere...

01:11:13.450 --> 01:11:16.330
That's why even with the police here investigating,

01:11:16.330 --> 01:11:20.040
they risked stealing the cutlass and the pistol anyway.

01:11:24.340 --> 01:11:25.880
The girl from the diving shop!

01:11:27.470 --> 01:11:28.800
What happened?

01:11:30.090 --> 01:11:31.760
Where's Mouri-san?

01:11:31.760 --> 01:11:33.100
He's not here.

01:11:33.100 --> 01:11:34.890
He should be at the police station right now.

01:11:34.890 --> 01:11:37.350
Ran-chan and Sonoko-chan have been kidnapped.

01:11:38.180 --> 01:11:39.390
They were taken away by boat.

01:11:39.390 --> 01:11:41.730
Who? Who kidnapped them?

01:11:43.020 --> 01:11:46.190
Matsumoto, the treasure hunter.

01:11:47.650 --> 01:11:50.110
They must be going to Yorioya Island!

01:11:50.860 --> 01:11:54.410
You guys, hurry and inform Uncle and the police.

01:11:54.410 --> 01:11:55.200
Got it.

01:12:02.250 --> 01:12:03.590
Be careful.

01:12:03.590 --> 01:12:04.380
Yep.

01:12:11.050 --> 01:12:12.390
Uncle,

01:12:13.550 --> 01:12:15.140
Can you take me out to sea?

01:12:15.140 --> 01:12:17.560
I need you to get me to that island.

01:12:17.560 --> 01:12:18.640
What?

01:12:18.980 --> 01:12:21.140
Not to find the treasure.

01:12:21.140 --> 01:12:23.310
I want to save Ran-neechan and her friend.

01:12:24.610 --> 01:12:26.190
Shinichi!

01:12:27.280 --> 01:12:28.400
Conan-kun,

01:12:28.400 --> 01:12:30.780
I heard that Ran-kun was kidnapped.

01:12:30.780 --> 01:12:31.780
Yeah.

01:12:33.320 --> 01:12:36.280
I know you're going to go save her, even if I tried to stop you.

01:12:37.290 --> 01:12:40.160
Hold on a second before you go. I want to give you something.

01:12:40.160 --> 01:12:42.710
I'll get the boat ready.

01:12:43.080 --> 01:12:44.080
Got it.

01:12:48.380 --> 01:12:50.760
Take these with you.

01:12:50.760 --> 01:12:52.760
These are mini-air tanks.

01:12:52.760 --> 01:12:56.890
Just pull, put in your mouth, you'll get 10 min worth of oxygen.

01:12:56.890 --> 01:12:59.180
Unfortunately, I only have two of them with me.

01:12:59.180 --> 01:13:01.270
So, save them for when you really need one.

01:13:02.190 --> 01:13:03.770
Thank you, professor.

01:13:10.530 --> 01:13:13.360
The two of you can share one air tank.

01:13:13.360 --> 01:13:16.370
You don't need us anymore! why don't you let us go?

01:13:16.370 --> 01:13:19.370
There's just one last thing I need from you...

01:13:21.750 --> 01:13:23.080
Hurry and get everything ready!

01:13:34.590 --> 01:13:36.050
Could it be...

01:13:37.510 --> 01:13:38.890
Sonoko!

01:13:41.060 --> 01:13:43.480
It's your turn, miss.

01:13:43.480 --> 01:13:45.900
What exactly do you want us to do?

01:13:45.900 --> 01:13:48.520
Don't worry, your turn's next.

01:13:52.360 --> 01:13:53.780
What?

01:13:53.780 --> 01:13:56.490
Ran and her friend were really kidnapped by Matsumoto?

01:13:56.490 --> 01:13:58.240
Where did they go?

01:13:58.240 --> 01:14:00.240
They went to an island, and island!

01:14:00.240 --> 01:14:01.580
It's called Yorioya Island.

01:14:01.580 --> 01:14:05.830
They figured out where the treasure is, and are going to get it now!

01:14:05.830 --> 01:14:07.290
Get ready to head out to the sea.

01:14:07.290 --> 01:14:08.960
I'm going to save them!

01:14:08.960 --> 01:14:10.380
Yes, sir!

01:14:14.760 --> 01:14:18.390
But, why did they take hostages with them?

01:14:18.390 --> 01:14:21.930
A hostage would only get in their way of finding the treasure.

01:14:21.930 --> 01:14:23.270
They have some other use for them.

01:14:23.270 --> 01:14:24.980
Another use?

01:14:24.980 --> 01:14:28.150
They were both injured by that rifle shot last night.

01:14:28.980 --> 01:14:33.690
The place they're going now is the same
 spot that the sharks attacked yesterday.

01:14:34.190 --> 01:14:36.320
They're going to be used as bait?!?

01:14:36.320 --> 01:14:37.610
Most likely.

01:14:47.040 --> 01:14:48.290
There it is!

01:15:04.390 --> 01:15:05.560
I knew it.

01:15:06.480 --> 01:15:08.770
What should we do!  there's not much time left.

01:15:09.100 --> 01:15:10.650
Continue on to Yorioya Island.

01:15:10.650 --> 01:15:11.730
What?!?

01:15:12.190 --> 01:15:15.280
I'm small enough to get through the entrance of the Two goddesses.

01:17:24.360 --> 01:17:25.160
Not good...

01:18:10.120 --> 01:18:11.620
Impressive.

01:18:11.620 --> 01:18:13.790
I can't believe you're still alive.

01:18:13.790 --> 01:18:16.670
Take these torches,

01:18:16.670 --> 01:18:18.380
or you won't be able to see anything inside the dark cavern.

01:18:18.960 --> 01:18:21.710
You'll only die if you stay here.

01:18:26.180 --> 01:18:27.840
Keep moving!

01:18:28.930 --> 01:18:30.220
Stop pushing me!

01:18:34.100 --> 01:18:35.020
This is...

01:18:35.810 --> 01:18:38.770
We've already been here a lot of times.

01:18:38.770 --> 01:18:43.480
We just <i>have</i> to find Anne Bonny and Mary Read's treasure today.

01:18:44.570 --> 01:18:47.240
You two, stay here. And don't you dare think of running away, either...

01:18:52.950 --> 01:18:56.290
There's a small temple straight ahead of you on that path.

01:18:56.660 --> 01:18:59.380
with statues of two goddesses by it.

01:18:59.380 --> 01:19:00.750
The entrance is behind them.

01:19:00.750 --> 01:19:01.880
Got it!

01:19:01.880 --> 01:19:03.760
You can only stay for 30 minutes,

01:19:03.760 --> 01:19:06.050
or the boat will be gone, and you won't be able to get back.

01:19:06.090 --> 01:19:07.590
Thanks!

01:19:07.590 --> 01:19:10.800
I'll go save Ran-neechan and Sonoko-neechan now!

01:19:17.440 --> 01:19:20.020
Anne Bonny and Mary Read, huh?

01:19:37.120 --> 01:19:38.540
This is weird...

01:19:38.540 --> 01:19:40.370
An adult should be able to fit through this...

01:19:40.670 --> 01:19:44.840
Last week, an earthquake caused a landslide which blocked the road.

01:19:45.460 --> 01:19:46.840
I see.

01:19:46.840 --> 01:19:48.880
The earthquake made the entrance bigger.

01:19:52.090 --> 01:19:53.640
Could they have taken Ran and...

01:19:54.010 --> 01:19:57.230
No, since they bothered to take them all the way here, I don't think they would kill them.

01:19:57.230 --> 01:19:58.350
But, what if...?

01:19:58.350 --> 01:20:02.230
What we do know is that Matsumoto was shot by a rifle last night.

01:20:04.150 --> 01:20:05.480
If they dive,

01:20:05.480 --> 01:20:08.610
the smell of blood would attract sharks.

01:20:08.610 --> 01:20:09.650
So, what does that mean?

01:20:10.910 --> 01:20:14.450
I means Ran-san and her friend might be used as bait.

01:20:16.790 --> 01:20:18.290
Wait a minute, Mouri-san!

01:20:18.290 --> 01:20:19.160
What are you doing?

01:20:19.160 --> 01:20:21.710
Let go of me! I can't just leave Ran in the hands of some scum-bags!

01:20:21.710 --> 01:20:23.290
It's impossible, Mouri-san!

01:20:23.290 --> 01:20:25.420
The storm's getting worse!

01:20:25.420 --> 01:20:27.460
Shut up! Let me go!

01:20:27.460 --> 01:20:28.510
I'm sorry I have to do this, but...

01:20:34.180 --> 01:20:35.890
What should we do now?

01:20:36.430 --> 01:20:38.470
We have to go back for now.

01:20:38.470 --> 01:20:40.140
I have a bad feeling about this, though.

01:20:46.110 --> 01:20:49.360
Hurry and come inside. It's really dangerous out here.

01:20:49.360 --> 01:20:51.700
But, they're in danger right now,

01:20:51.700 --> 01:20:55.320
Conan-kun, Ran-oneesan, and Sonoko-neesan.

01:20:55.320 --> 01:20:56.160
Yeah.

01:20:56.160 --> 01:20:56.990
That's right.

01:21:04.790 --> 01:21:06.540
The water level's gone down some.

01:21:06.540 --> 01:21:08.300
The tide is ebbing right now.

01:21:08.300 --> 01:21:09.840
Are we going into that cave?

01:21:09.840 --> 01:21:11.720
That's right.

01:21:11.720 --> 01:21:15.260
It's a shortcut to the treasure.

01:21:15.260 --> 01:21:18.470
Okay, bring two air tanks.

01:21:35.780 --> 01:21:39.370
So, the legend of the pirates was true...

01:21:39.660 --> 01:21:41.080
I guess so...

01:21:56.220 --> 01:21:57.970
Put the air tanks down. You're going in first.

01:21:59.140 --> 01:22:00.010
But...

01:22:00.010 --> 01:22:01.430
Shut up, and get moving!

01:22:13.820 --> 01:22:15.950
Bones! Bones! Bones!

01:22:17.530 --> 01:22:19.740
Looks like everything's safe this time around.

01:22:20.790 --> 01:22:22.040
The gas is gone...

01:22:22.040 --> 01:22:22.910
Gas?

01:22:22.910 --> 01:22:27.000
This place is full of gas when the wind isn't blowing as hard.

01:22:27.580 --> 01:22:29.590
That's why you told us to go first?

01:22:30.290 --> 01:22:33.550
Why else would we need you here?

01:22:33.550 --> 01:22:34.420
Hurry, and keep going.

01:22:43.470 --> 01:22:44.770
What?

01:22:44.770 --> 01:22:45.980
This is it!

01:22:48.650 --> 01:22:50.110
We finally found it!

01:22:53.400 --> 01:22:55.190
What an idiot...

01:22:55.190 --> 01:22:57.700
Who asked you to put this in to open it?

01:22:57.700 --> 01:22:59.450
That's why you died.

01:23:00.200 --> 01:23:01.450
You need to use this.

01:23:13.960 --> 01:23:15.420
You, open it!

01:23:15.420 --> 01:23:16.550
Me?

01:23:16.550 --> 01:23:17.970
Let me do it.

01:23:29.350 --> 01:23:30.400
Ran!

01:23:30.400 --> 01:23:32.610
Shit, it's not working after all?

01:23:41.820 --> 01:23:43.330
Just give it up, already!

01:23:45.080 --> 01:23:47.870
So that's what it is.

01:23:47.870 --> 01:23:49.170
Do you know how to open it?

01:23:49.170 --> 01:23:53.710
Anne and Mary always fought back-to-back.

01:23:53.710 --> 01:23:55.130
Which means...

01:23:56.130 --> 01:23:57.800
...they should be put this way.

01:24:15.520 --> 01:24:17.690
We found it, we found it!

01:24:21.240 --> 01:24:22.660
Give me the torch!

01:24:42.340 --> 01:24:43.680
It's amazing...

01:24:43.680 --> 01:24:44.600
The treasure...

01:24:44.600 --> 01:24:45.890
Where's the treasure?!

01:24:49.060 --> 01:24:50.770
Be patient!

01:24:51.980 --> 01:24:54.110
Ran, what should we do now?

01:24:54.110 --> 01:24:56.190
We could run away now,

01:24:56.190 --> 01:24:59.440
but we don't have an air tank, so we'd drown
 before ever getting to the surface.

01:24:59.740 --> 01:25:00.740
You're right.

01:25:01.280 --> 01:25:04.410
So, we just have to try and hold them on 
until someone comes and saves us.

01:25:04.410 --> 01:25:05.620
That's right.

01:25:11.540 --> 01:25:12.670
There's wind.

01:25:12.670 --> 01:25:13.540
There's an opening around here!

01:25:14.290 --> 01:25:15.080
Dammit!

01:25:16.000 --> 01:25:18.670
Where is it? Where is this freaking treasure at?

01:25:18.670 --> 01:25:22.470
It's the same for me! 
I can't find even a single piece of treasure anywhere!

01:25:22.720 --> 01:25:24.300
Not even a coin!

01:25:24.300 --> 01:25:28.260
I don't know how, but someone must have gotten here before us.

01:25:28.260 --> 01:25:30.020
Hey, this is different from what we talked about!

01:25:30.020 --> 01:25:32.850
I came all the way here because 
you told me there would be treasure!

01:25:32.850 --> 01:25:34.520
Shut up!

01:25:37.400 --> 01:25:41.610
There's no helping it then.
We better get out of here before air runs out.

01:25:41.610 --> 01:25:45.410
Yeah, but first, let's get rid of the dead-weight.

01:25:50.200 --> 01:25:54.540
Sorry, but this is how it ends for you.

01:25:55.290 --> 01:25:56.380
Don't come any closer!

01:25:56.380 --> 01:25:58.500
Ran, I trust you to watch my back.

01:25:58.500 --> 01:26:00.170
Be careful, Sonoko!

01:26:04.550 --> 01:26:05.720
Bitch!

01:26:15.350 --> 01:26:18.190
Damn, this woman sure is a fighter.

01:26:18.940 --> 01:26:20.690
Indeed.

01:26:21.190 --> 01:26:25.450
But, no matter how good the are, they can't do anything...

01:26:25.450 --> 01:26:27.320
...against this!

01:26:29.330 --> 01:26:32.290
Always play your trump card last.

01:26:40.880 --> 01:26:42.420
Both of you, get down!

01:26:51.350 --> 01:26:52.560
Are you okay...

01:26:53.890 --> 01:26:55.680
...Ran-neechan, Sonoko-neechan?

01:26:56.350 --> 01:26:58.310
What a relief you came, you brave boy!

01:26:58.310 --> 01:27:00.900
But, how did you get all the way down here?

01:27:00.900 --> 01:27:02.650
There's a tunnel that leads here from Yorioya Island.

01:27:03.530 --> 01:27:07.110
So, the pirates' treasure really does exist?

01:27:08.320 --> 01:27:09.870
There's no treasure here.

01:27:10.240 --> 01:27:13.790
They said that it was taken by someone who found this place before us.

01:27:15.290 --> 01:27:16.830
Did you hear that?

01:27:16.830 --> 01:27:17.870
Isn't that a shame?

01:27:19.080 --> 01:27:21.000
You can stop hiding now.

01:27:21.500 --> 01:27:24.420
You were sneaking behind me, and following me all the way down here, weren't you?

01:27:33.060 --> 01:27:36.430
Inspector Megure, we can go out to sea now!

01:27:36.430 --> 01:27:38.690
The wind is dying down now!

01:27:38.690 --> 01:27:39.770
Mouri-san.

01:27:39.770 --> 01:27:44.400
The weather forecast said that the storm won't stop until morning.

01:27:44.400 --> 01:27:46.150
But... Look...

01:27:46.150 --> 01:27:48.490
The storm is really calming down now.

01:27:48.490 --> 01:27:50.240
Calm down, Mouri-san.

01:27:50.240 --> 01:27:52.370
How can I calm down?

01:27:52.370 --> 01:27:54.490
Ran has been kidnapped,

01:27:54.490 --> 01:27:58.580
and I have to put my faith in a brat to go save her!

01:27:58.580 --> 01:28:02.000
All the while, we adults have to just sit and do nothing!

01:28:02.000 --> 01:28:03.040
Mouri-kun,

01:28:03.710 --> 01:28:08.880
I understand how you feel, but there's nothing we can do, if we can't go out to sea.

01:28:10.130 --> 01:28:12.010
Once the storm calms,

01:28:12.010 --> 01:28:14.350
We'll go save Ran at once.

01:28:14.350 --> 01:28:16.140
Now, be patient.

01:28:17.770 --> 01:28:19.140
Damn it!

01:28:22.440 --> 01:28:24.860
You can stop hiding now.

01:28:24.860 --> 01:28:27.480
You were sneaking behind me, and following me all the way down here, weren't you?

01:28:28.030 --> 01:28:29.530
Iwanaga-san.

01:28:34.120 --> 01:28:35.870
Now, now...

01:28:35.870 --> 01:28:38.250
Saying that I was "sneaking" is a little too harsh.

01:28:38.250 --> 01:28:41.370
Just like you, I wanted to save them.

01:28:41.370 --> 01:28:43.380
Then, why are you carrying a rifle with you?

01:28:43.710 --> 01:28:47.420
I heard that they were international fugitives.

01:28:47.840 --> 01:28:50.920
That's the rifle that belongs to Mineo-san, right?

01:28:51.470 --> 01:28:53.010
N-No...

01:28:53.010 --> 01:28:56.220
You brought the rifle with you because you were afraid of the treasure being stolen.

01:28:56.220 --> 01:28:58.310
This has nothing to do with the treasure!

01:29:00.560 --> 01:29:01.940
Iwanaga-san,

01:29:02.310 --> 01:29:07.690
you told us you thought of all those hints on the cards yourself, right?

01:29:07.690 --> 01:29:09.110
Uh, yeah...

01:29:09.440 --> 01:29:14.740
But I saw the exact same numerical hint in Mima-san's house.

01:29:14.740 --> 01:29:17.330
It was on a three-hundred year old map,

01:29:18.160 --> 01:29:21.080
which I heard was left by Anne Bonny herself.

01:29:22.790 --> 01:29:26.920
In other words, you saw that map before, but couldn't figure out its clues.

01:29:27.630 --> 01:29:31.090
So, you used the map's clues to invent a game for tourists who came to the island...

01:29:31.550 --> 01:29:35.760
so they could help you solve the clues, right?

01:29:35.760 --> 01:29:37.050
Oh, yeah!

01:29:37.050 --> 01:29:40.890
You even tried to get my dad to join in the treasure hunt game too!

01:29:40.890 --> 01:29:41.680
I see!

01:29:41.980 --> 01:29:46.940
The probability of a famous detective solving the clues is much higher than a bunch of kids.

01:29:46.940 --> 01:29:51.030
In order to track the movements 
of the people taking part in the treasure hunt,

01:29:51.030 --> 01:29:54.150
you installed GPS trackers on the rental bikes, right?

01:29:54.660 --> 01:29:57.700
Th-That's because I was worried that those who participated might run into danger.

01:29:57.700 --> 01:30:01.580
If change the numbers on the map into the letters of the alphabet,

01:30:01.580 --> 01:30:05.170
they spell out "Jolly Roger", referring to a pirate flag.

01:30:05.620 --> 01:30:10.170
If you looked at Yorioya island from above, it looked like a skull.

01:30:10.170 --> 01:30:12.380
That's why Anne Bonny left such a hint.

01:30:12.970 --> 01:30:16.430
Also, even the pronunciation of Yorioya Island,

01:30:16.430 --> 01:30:18.640
came from the pronunciation of the words "Jolly Roger".

01:30:20.100 --> 01:30:23.930
I'm sure you already knew about this,

01:30:23.930 --> 01:30:26.770
but there's another meaning behind the "Jolly Roger".

01:30:26.770 --> 01:30:27.900
What is it?

01:30:28.690 --> 01:30:34.240
You know how the real map has the pirate flag, or Jolly Roger, on it?

01:30:34.240 --> 01:30:37.990
The teeth of the skull gave the second hint,

01:30:38.740 --> 01:30:40.580
"Dos Diosas."

01:30:40.580 --> 01:30:42.870
The hint is "Two goddesses".

01:30:43.540 --> 01:30:44.710
Conan-kun?

01:30:46.040 --> 01:30:47.040
That's right,

01:30:47.040 --> 01:30:49.840
you should have seen it when you followed me just now,

01:30:50.420 --> 01:30:52.960
the temple with the statues of two goddesses.

01:30:53.510 --> 01:30:55.800
That's the entrance.

01:30:56.930 --> 01:30:58.180
I see.

01:30:58.590 --> 01:31:00.140
How did you know?

01:31:00.850 --> 01:31:02.010
Damn it,

01:31:02.010 --> 01:31:04.180
was my guess wrong from the very beginning?

01:31:07.190 --> 01:31:09.980
The rigged BC jacket,

01:31:09.980 --> 01:31:12.900
and the rifle attack on the treasure hunters...

01:31:12.900 --> 01:31:14.690
You did all of those, didn't you?

01:31:15.070 --> 01:31:17.200
There were tire marks left by your bike...

01:31:17.200 --> 01:31:22.330
both behind the cave, and at the place where the bullet shells from the rifle were found.

01:31:24.910 --> 01:31:28.120
I made mistakes that even an grade-schooler noticed...

01:31:28.920 --> 01:31:30.580
It wasn't a grade-schooler.

01:31:33.460 --> 01:31:35.460
Uncle Kogoro told me.

01:31:35.760 --> 01:31:38.630
He told me all this,

01:31:38.630 --> 01:31:43.390
and he noticed how Iwanaga-san had the smell of gunpowder on him.

01:31:43.850 --> 01:31:50.230
It's probably because it's an old rifle which doesn't work as well, so the gunpowder flies all over the place.

01:31:50.230 --> 01:31:51.520
I get it now.

01:31:51.520 --> 01:31:52.480
I should've known.

01:31:53.650 --> 01:31:56.190
As expected of the famous detective, Mouri Kogoro.

01:31:59.110 --> 01:32:00.410
E-Earthquake?

01:32:03.530 --> 01:32:04.540
It stopped.

01:32:07.000 --> 01:32:08.790
This isn't good! We need to get out of here fast!

01:32:08.790 --> 01:32:11.080
Yeah, let's bring them out.

01:32:13.920 --> 01:32:15.630
Give me a hand, Iwanaga-san!

01:32:15.630 --> 01:32:16.630
Okay.

01:32:23.760 --> 01:32:24.810
Damn it!

01:32:25.260 --> 01:32:27.270
What should we do? The rock blocked the entrance!

01:32:29.520 --> 01:32:30.560
It's gas!

01:32:30.850 --> 01:32:32.230
Get to the boat!

01:32:32.650 --> 01:32:33.690
Hurry!

01:32:48.540 --> 01:32:50.540
Damn, if this continues...

01:32:50.960 --> 01:32:53.790
Conan-kun, what should we do now?

01:32:53.790 --> 01:32:57.050
Bring them to the cabin, just in case.

01:32:57.050 --> 01:32:59.920
Hook an air tank up to them so they can get some oxygen,

01:32:59.920 --> 01:33:01.760
and don't let them breathe in the gas.

01:33:02.050 --> 01:33:04.640
Ran-neechan, you two could use these.

01:33:05.760 --> 01:33:06.850
What are these?

01:33:07.180 --> 01:33:10.180
They're mini-air tanks that professor Agasa invented.

01:33:10.180 --> 01:33:11.350
What about you?

01:33:11.350 --> 01:33:14.060
I have another one right here. Don't worry!

01:33:15.520 --> 01:33:16.520
Is that so...?

01:33:25.870 --> 01:33:27.370
Damn, what do I do now?

01:33:27.740 --> 01:33:29.290
If this goes on, the gas will...

01:33:30.500 --> 01:33:31.540
Gas?

01:33:34.460 --> 01:33:36.460
The gas is probably methane.

01:33:37.090 --> 01:33:39.090
It probably rose and accumulated at the top of the cave.

01:33:39.760 --> 01:33:41.550
If we can make use of the gas...

01:33:42.220 --> 01:33:44.510
Is there anything, anything at all?

01:33:46.510 --> 01:33:47.600
That'll work!

01:33:48.560 --> 01:33:50.770
Ran-neechan, Sonoko-neechan,

01:33:50.770 --> 01:33:52.100
Please, listen to me.

01:33:53.140 --> 01:33:55.650
Since the water flowing into this place broke through,

01:33:55.650 --> 01:33:57.900
the walls probably aren't very thick.

01:33:57.900 --> 01:34:02.190
That's why, I think if we make the gas explode, we can make an opening in the top of the cave so the ship can...

01:34:03.110 --> 01:34:06.660
You want us to ride the ship out to escape?

01:34:06.660 --> 01:34:07.660
Will we be alright?

01:34:08.370 --> 01:34:09.200
I don't know...

01:34:09.660 --> 01:34:14.500
But, we'll all drown or be poisoned by the gas if we don't get out soon.

01:34:15.210 --> 01:34:16.120
We'll die anyway.

01:34:17.880 --> 01:34:19.840
We might as well give it a try.

01:34:21.250 --> 01:34:22.760
What are you going to do, Conan-kun?

01:34:23.840 --> 01:34:28.970
I'm going to kick that chain fragment
 at the rocks at the top of the cave.

01:34:29.510 --> 01:34:31.310
It'll create a spark,

01:34:31.310 --> 01:34:33.430
Which should be able to make the gas explode.

01:34:33.430 --> 01:34:37.100
Ran-neechan, you two go into the cabin 
and breathe through the air tanks.

01:34:37.100 --> 01:34:40.980
When the gas explodes,
 all of the oxygen in the air will be gone in an instant.

01:34:42.230 --> 01:34:43.490
What about you?

01:34:43.490 --> 01:34:44.900
I'll be fine...

01:34:44.900 --> 01:34:48.280
As soon as I kick the chain, I'll jump into the cabin along with you.

01:34:48.280 --> 01:34:49.320
Don't worry.

01:34:57.830 --> 01:34:59.040
I got it.

01:35:07.590 --> 01:35:08.550
Inspector...

01:35:09.720 --> 01:35:11.300
Get the ship ready!

01:35:11.300 --> 01:35:12.310
We're heading out to sea!

01:35:12.640 --> 01:35:13.770
Yes, sir!

01:35:31.740 --> 01:35:33.740
Everything's prepared and okay, Conan-kun!

01:35:39.620 --> 01:35:40.750
Yes!

01:36:40.190 --> 01:36:40.940
This is bad!

01:36:59.750 --> 01:37:00.750
Conan-kun...

01:37:01.540 --> 01:37:02.620
Conan-kun!

01:37:03.750 --> 01:37:05.170
Hang on, Conan-kun!

01:37:08.170 --> 01:37:09.090
Ran...

01:37:17.140 --> 01:37:18.720
Hurry up, hurry up!

01:37:18.720 --> 01:37:20.600
Full speed!

01:37:38.830 --> 01:37:40.910
A-A pirate ship?!?

01:37:57.350 --> 01:37:58.510
Ran!

01:37:59.310 --> 01:38:01.640
Ran, are you alright?

01:38:01.640 --> 01:38:03.810
I'm fine!

01:38:03.810 --> 01:38:04.810
We're saved!

01:38:17.950 --> 01:38:19.330
Everyone, get off the boat!

01:38:19.990 --> 01:38:21.080
Watch out!

01:38:21.080 --> 01:38:22.660
Jump into the ocean!

01:38:22.660 --> 01:38:23.460
Sonoko!

01:38:26.830 --> 01:38:28.210
This way!

01:38:50.860 --> 01:38:53.610
So, did you find the treasure?

01:38:53.610 --> 01:38:54.690
Nope.

01:38:54.690 --> 01:38:57.410
There was just this wreck of a pirate ship.

01:38:57.410 --> 01:38:59.120
Maybe that ship was the treasure

01:38:59.950 --> 01:39:03.620
The map that Anne Bonny left behind...

01:39:03.620 --> 01:39:05.910
...wasn't a map leading to treasure.

01:39:05.910 --> 01:39:11.130
She was just trying to send a message to Mary Read, who was in jail.

01:39:11.670 --> 01:39:13.170
A message?

01:39:13.170 --> 01:39:14.760
I'm right here!

01:39:14.760 --> 01:39:19.050
I'll always be here waiting for you, Shinichi!

01:39:19.050 --> 01:39:20.350
Just kidding...

01:39:20.350 --> 01:39:21.600
Sonoko!

01:39:23.890 --> 01:39:27.190
Who do you think you are, acting like a know-it-all?

01:39:27.190 --> 01:39:30.900
No, there's a strong possibility that he's right.

01:39:32.610 --> 01:39:37.990
Most likely, Anne built that ship and stored it there for Mary,

01:39:37.990 --> 01:39:41.570
in preparation for the day 
when they could go back out to sea together.

01:39:41.780 --> 01:39:43.950
That's why she built the ship.

01:39:44.450 --> 01:39:50.790
However, Mary fell sick in prison,
 and passed away before that could happen.

01:39:50.790 --> 01:39:55.420
Anne continues to wait for her partner, Mary, 
until the day she died as well.

01:39:55.800 --> 01:39:58.800
The ship that was left behind,

01:39:58.800 --> 01:40:05.720
ended up in a cave at the bottom of the ocean, waiting for the day to come where it could set sail with its builder.

01:40:05.890 --> 01:40:07.850
And now, three hundred years later,

01:40:07.850 --> 01:40:10.980
it finally had its first and final voyage.

01:40:10.980 --> 01:40:18.900
It sent all of you to the surface, then crumbled and vanished, just like the people who built it.

01:40:20.200 --> 01:40:22.870
I'm just guessing though.

01:40:22.870 --> 01:40:23.870
So, don't take it seriously.

01:40:28.540 --> 01:40:34.040
It's been three hundred years, though, 
so it's unlikely we'll ever know the truth.

01:40:34.040 --> 01:40:39.300
No, I don't doubt that Anne was waiting for Mary, Uncle.

01:40:39.300 --> 01:40:43.010
The proof is below the skull of the Jolly Roger...

01:40:48.730 --> 01:40:52.150
Anne and Mary's pistol and cutlass.

